WEBVTT

00:07.258 --> 00:09.926
BARTON: Okay, hold on,
don't shoot.

00:11.012 --> 00:12.763
- You see where you're going?
- Mm-hmm.

00:12.930 --> 00:13.930
Okay.

00:14.098 --> 00:16.016
Now, let's worry
about how you get there.

00:16.893 --> 00:18.268
Gotta move your foot here.

00:18.770 --> 00:20.187
Point your toe this way.

00:20.563 --> 00:22.105
Your hips here.

00:22.315 --> 00:23.648
Okay?

00:24.442 --> 00:25.901
- Can you see?
- Yeah.

00:25.985 --> 00:27.068
- Are you sure?
- Mm-hmm.

00:27.153 --> 00:28.487
How about now?
Can you see now?

00:28.571 --> 00:29.905
- (CHUCKLES) No.
- How about now?

00:29.989 --> 00:31.364
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:32.074 --> 00:33.158
All right.

00:33.826 --> 00:35.744
Ready? Three fingers.

00:36.496 --> 00:37.621
COOPER: Nice!

00:39.207 --> 00:40.791
LAURA: Nice throw, kiddo.

00:40.958 --> 00:42.042
COOPER: Here you go.

00:42.418 --> 00:44.544
Hey, you guys want mayo?
Or mustard?

00:44.629 --> 00:46.087
Or both?

00:46.380 --> 00:48.340
Who puts mayo on a hot dog?

00:48.508 --> 00:49.549
Probably your brothers.

00:49.634 --> 00:51.718
Uh, two mustard, please!
Thanks, Mama.

00:51.803 --> 00:52.803
LAURA: Got it!

00:53.262 --> 00:54.805
Nate, mayo or mustard?

00:55.515 --> 00:56.723
How about ketchup?

00:57.141 --> 00:59.100
LAURA: Or ketchup.
I got ketchup, too.

00:59.393 --> 01:00.477
BARTON: Mind your elbow.

01:02.563 --> 01:04.523
(LAUGHS) Good job, hawk-eye.

01:04.690 --> 01:07.400
Go get your arrow. (CHUCKLES)

01:09.529 --> 01:10.529
LAURA: Hey, guys!

01:10.696 --> 01:12.906
Enough practice.
Soup's on!

01:13.074 --> 01:14.115
BARTON: All right.

01:14.283 --> 01:15.575
We're coming. We're hungry.

01:16.661 --> 01:18.203
Lila, let's go.

01:21.249 --> 01:22.499
Lila?

01:25.419 --> 01:26.419
Honey?

01:30.299 --> 01:31.383
Hey, babe?

01:40.268 --> 01:42.269
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)
- Babe?

01:44.313 --> 01:45.605
Babe?

01:46.566 --> 01:48.441
(WHISTLES) Boys!

01:50.194 --> 01:51.194
Boys!

01:53.531 --> 01:54.656
Laura!

01:54.824 --> 01:56.825
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

02:00.454 --> 02:02.706
(PSYCHEDELIC ROCK SONG
PLAYING)

02:37.283 --> 02:38.575
- (GRUNTS)
- (OBJECT CLATTERS)

02:38.659 --> 02:39.701
You don't need to do that.

02:40.244 --> 02:42.913
Because, uh, you're just
holding the position.

02:43.956 --> 02:45.206
- Oh, yeah.
- (GRUNTS)

02:45.416 --> 02:47.292
- That was close.
- (GRUNTS)

02:48.294 --> 02:50.045
That's a goal.
We are now one apiece.

02:50.212 --> 02:51.588
I would like to try again.

02:54.050 --> 02:56.301
We're tied up.
Feel the tension?

02:56.469 --> 02:58.011
It's fun.

02:58.179 --> 03:00.180
That was terrible.
Now you have a chance to win.

03:01.432 --> 03:02.432
And you've won.

03:03.517 --> 03:04.684
Congratulations.

03:04.852 --> 03:05.977
Fair game.

03:07.396 --> 03:08.688
Good sport.

03:09.690 --> 03:11.066
You have fun?

03:12.902 --> 03:14.819
It was fun.

03:33.130 --> 03:34.589
- (CLICKS)
- (GRUNTS)

03:34.674 --> 03:36.049
(HELMET WHIRRING)

03:36.133 --> 03:37.342
(SIGHS)

03:37.426 --> 03:38.969
This thing on?

03:41.138 --> 03:43.139
Hey, Miss Potts. Pep.

03:44.475 --> 03:47.185
(EXHALES DEEPLY)
If you find this recording...

03:47.353 --> 03:50.105
don't post it on social media.

03:50.189 --> 03:51.898
It's gonna be
a real tearjerker.

03:52.566 --> 03:54.985
I don't know if
you're ever gonna see these.

03:55.152 --> 03:57.195
I don't even know
if you're still...

03:57.738 --> 03:59.614
Oh, God, I hope so.

04:00.449 --> 04:02.701
<i>Today's day 21.</i>

04:02.868 --> 04:05.120
<i>No, uh, 22.</i>

04:05.788 --> 04:08.331
<i>You know, if it wasn't</i>
<i>for the existential terror...</i>

04:08.499 --> 04:10.667
<i>of staring into</i>
<i>the literal void of space,</i>

04:10.751 --> 04:12.961
<i>I'd say I'm feeling</i>
<i>a little better today.</i>

04:13.129 --> 04:14.546
<i>Infection's run its course,</i>

04:14.630 --> 04:16.172
<i>thanks to</i>
<i>the Blue Meanie back there.</i>

04:16.757 --> 04:18.341
<i>Oh, you'd love her.</i>

04:18.509 --> 04:19.926
<i>Very practical.</i>

04:20.386 --> 04:22.470
<i>Only a tiny bit sadistic.</i>

04:27.476 --> 04:29.644
<i>So, the fuel cells</i>
<i>were cracked during battle...</i>

04:29.729 --> 04:31.896
<i>and we figured out a way</i>
<i>to reverse the ion charge...</i>

04:32.064 --> 04:34.774
<i>and bought ourselves</i>
<i>about 48 hours of flight time.</i>

04:38.154 --> 04:39.904
<i>Uh, but it's now dead</i>
<i>in the water.</i>

04:40.072 --> 04:43.575
<i>Thousand light years</i>
<i>from the nearest 7-Eleven.</i>

04:45.077 --> 04:47.454
<i>Oxygen will run out</i>
<i>tomorrow morning...</i>

04:48.956 --> 04:50.623
<i>and that'll be it.</i>

04:53.919 --> 04:57.005
<i>Pep, I know I said</i>
<i>no more surprises...</i>

04:57.173 --> 04:58.882
<i>but I gotta say</i>
<i>I was really hoping</i>

04:58.966 --> 05:00.759
<i>to pull off one last one.</i>

05:00.926 --> 05:02.886
<i>But it looks like...</i>

05:03.054 --> 05:04.846
<i>Well, you know</i>
<i>what it looks like.</i>

05:06.265 --> 05:08.099
Don't feel bad about this.

05:08.267 --> 05:11.061
I mean, actually, if you
grovel for a couple weeks...

05:11.812 --> 05:14.939
and then move on
with enormous guilt...

05:20.071 --> 05:22.072
I should probably lie down
for a minute.

05:22.156 --> 05:24.115
Go rest my eyes.

05:24.492 --> 05:25.658
(SIGHS)

05:27.119 --> 05:28.661
Please know...

05:29.872 --> 05:33.458
when I drift off, it'll be
like every night lately.

05:33.667 --> 05:36.628
I'm fine. Totally fine.

05:37.296 --> 05:38.588
I dream about you.

05:40.174 --> 05:41.758
Because it's always you.

05:45.471 --> 05:47.138
(CLICKS, POWERS OFF)

05:53.938 --> 05:55.522
(GROANING SOFTLY)

06:05.574 --> 06:07.408
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

07:29.700 --> 07:30.950
(DISTANT BOOM)

08:19.625 --> 08:21.417
(RUMBLING)

09:01.000 --> 09:02.959
(TONY PANTING)

09:04.503 --> 09:05.503
Couldn't stop him.

09:05.671 --> 09:06.671
Neither could I.

09:06.839 --> 09:08.006
Hang on.

09:10.426 --> 09:12.010
I lost the kid.

09:14.555 --> 09:16.139
Tony, we lost.

09:18.434 --> 09:19.434
Is, uh...?

09:20.436 --> 09:22.061
- Oh, good.
- Oh, my God!

09:23.063 --> 09:24.731
Oh, my God! (SOBBING)

09:29.528 --> 09:31.237
It's okay.

09:37.619 --> 09:39.954
RHODES: It's been 23 days
since Thanos came to Earth.

09:42.458 --> 09:44.751
NATASHA: World governments
are in pieces.

09:45.044 --> 09:46.711
The parts
that are still working...

09:47.212 --> 09:50.715
...are trying to take a census
and it looks like he did...

09:53.469 --> 09:55.053
He did exactly what he said
he was gonna do.

09:55.220 --> 09:56.304
Thanos wiped out...

09:58.807 --> 10:01.893
...50% of
all living creatures.

10:06.231 --> 10:08.149
Where is he now? Where?

10:08.317 --> 10:10.026
We don't know.

10:10.194 --> 10:13.279
He just opened a portal
and walked through.

10:14.281 --> 10:15.448
(SIGHS)

10:15.908 --> 10:16.949
What's wrong with him?

10:18.035 --> 10:19.994
ROCKET: Oh, he's pissed.

10:20.162 --> 10:21.496
He thinks he failed.

10:22.956 --> 10:24.040
Which, of course, he did...

10:24.124 --> 10:26.250
but there's a lot of that
going around, ain't there?

10:26.418 --> 10:27.835
Honestly,
until this exact second

10:27.920 --> 10:29.045
I thought you were
a Build-A-Bear.

10:29.213 --> 10:30.630
Maybe I am.

10:30.714 --> 10:32.173
We've been hunting Thanos
for three weeks now.

10:32.257 --> 10:34.258
Deep space scans...

10:34.510 --> 10:36.469
and satellites,
and we got nothing.

10:38.263 --> 10:39.263
Tony, you fought him.

10:39.348 --> 10:40.348
Who told you that?

10:41.016 --> 10:42.058
I didn't fight him.

10:42.226 --> 10:43.893
No, he wiped my face
with a planet...

10:43.977 --> 10:45.144
while the Bleecker Street
magician

10:45.229 --> 10:46.479
gave away the store.

10:46.563 --> 10:47.563
That's what happened.

10:47.648 --> 10:48.981
There was no fight,
'cause he's not beatable.

10:49.066 --> 10:51.776
Did he give you any clues,
any coordinates, anything?

10:51.860 --> 10:53.277
Uh... (SPUTTERS)

10:54.780 --> 10:56.280
I saw this coming
a few years back.

10:56.448 --> 10:58.074
I had a vision.
I didn't wanna believe it.

10:58.575 --> 11:00.034
Thought I was dreaming.

11:00.202 --> 11:01.202
Tony, I'm gonna need you
to focus.

11:01.370 --> 11:03.121
And I needed you.

11:03.288 --> 11:04.330
As in, past tense.

11:04.498 --> 11:07.750
That trumps what you need.
It's too late, buddy.

11:07.918 --> 11:09.043
Sorry.

11:09.753 --> 11:12.713
(SNIFFS) You know what I need?
I need a shave.

11:13.382 --> 11:15.800
And I believe I remember
telling all youse...

11:15.884 --> 11:17.009
Tony, Tony!

11:17.094 --> 11:20.471
...alive and otherwise,
that what we needed

11:20.556 --> 11:22.432
was a suit of armor
around the world.

11:22.516 --> 11:23.516
Remember that?

11:23.600 --> 11:26.269
Whether it impacted
our precious freedoms or not.

11:26.353 --> 11:27.562
That's what we needed.

11:27.729 --> 11:28.813
Well, that didn't work out,
did it?

11:28.981 --> 11:30.398
I said we'd lose.

11:30.566 --> 11:32.733
You said,
"We'll do that together, too."

11:33.277 --> 11:34.360
And guess what, Cap?

11:34.528 --> 11:35.820
We lost.

11:36.280 --> 11:37.280
And you weren't there.

11:38.866 --> 11:40.032
But that's what we do, right?

11:40.200 --> 11:43.035
Our best work after the fact?
We're the "Avengers."

11:43.120 --> 11:45.163
We're the "Avengers,"
not the "Pre-vengers."

11:45.247 --> 11:46.247
- Okay.
- Right?

11:46.331 --> 11:47.582
You made your point.
Just sit down, okay?

11:47.666 --> 11:48.833
Okay. No, no, here's my point.
You know what?

11:48.917 --> 11:50.376
- She's great by the way.
- Tony, you're sick. Sit down.

11:50.461 --> 11:52.170
TONY: We need you.
You're new blood.

11:52.254 --> 11:55.173
Bunch of tired old mules.
I got nothing for you, Cap.

11:55.257 --> 11:56.549
I got no coordinates...

11:56.717 --> 11:59.469
no clues, no strategies,
no options.

11:59.636 --> 12:01.345
Zero. Zip. Nada.

12:01.513 --> 12:03.264
No trust, liar.

12:05.851 --> 12:07.268
(TONY BREATHING SHAKILY)

12:07.811 --> 12:09.061
Here, take this.

12:09.229 --> 12:11.355
You find him,
you put that on...

12:11.815 --> 12:13.357
you hide.

12:14.651 --> 12:16.360
- STEVE: Tony!
- I'm fine.

12:16.528 --> 12:18.237
Let me...

12:24.745 --> 12:26.037
RHODES: Bruce gave him
a sedative.

12:26.205 --> 12:27.914
He's gonna probably be out
for the rest of the day.

12:28.999 --> 12:30.458
CAROL: You guys
take care of him...

12:30.626 --> 12:32.168
and I'll bring him a Xorrian
elixir when I come back.

12:32.753 --> 12:33.753
Where are you going?

12:33.921 --> 12:35.588
To kill Thanos.

12:38.634 --> 12:39.842
NATASHA: Hey.

12:39.927 --> 12:42.053
You know, we usually work
as a team here...

12:42.221 --> 12:43.888
and, uh, between you and I,
morale's a little fragile.

12:44.056 --> 12:46.474
We realize up there
is more your territory,

12:46.558 --> 12:47.642
but this is our fight, too.

12:47.809 --> 12:48.976
You even know where he is?

12:49.144 --> 12:50.311
I know people who might.

12:50.479 --> 12:51.812
NEBULA: Don't bother.

12:52.773 --> 12:54.524
I can tell you
where Thanos is.

12:57.069 --> 13:00.029
Thanos spent a long time
trying to perfect me.

13:00.656 --> 13:04.700
And when he worked, he talked
about his Great Plan.

13:04.868 --> 13:07.954
Even disassembled,
I wanted to please him.

13:08.121 --> 13:09.539
I'd ask...

13:10.082 --> 13:12.750
where would we go
once his plan was complete?

13:13.252 --> 13:15.253
And his answer
was always the same.

13:19.466 --> 13:20.466
"To the Garden."

13:21.134 --> 13:23.844
That's cute.
Thanos has a retirement plan.

13:24.012 --> 13:25.555
So, where is he?

13:25.847 --> 13:27.974
When Thanos snapped
his fingers...

13:28.141 --> 13:30.142
Earth became ground zero
for a power surge

13:30.227 --> 13:32.019
of ridiculously
cosmic proportions.

13:32.187 --> 13:34.397
No one's ever seen
anything like it.

13:34.565 --> 13:35.898
Until two days ago...

13:37.734 --> 13:39.318
on this planet.

13:40.028 --> 13:41.529
Thanos is there.

13:43.240 --> 13:44.949
He used the stones again.

13:45.200 --> 13:46.951
BANNER: Hey, hey, hey.
(CHUCKLES)

13:47.035 --> 13:48.995
We'd be going in shorthanded,
you know?

13:49.162 --> 13:50.621
RHODES: Look, he's still
got the stones, so...

13:50.706 --> 13:52.248
So, let's get 'em.

13:52.416 --> 13:53.874
Use them
to bring everyone back.

13:53.959 --> 13:55.126
BANNER: Just like that?

13:55.210 --> 13:56.794
Yeah. Just like that.

13:56.962 --> 14:00.131
Even if there's a small chance
that we can undo this...

14:00.299 --> 14:03.009
I mean, we owe it to everyone
who's not in this room to try.

14:03.176 --> 14:04.802
If we do this, how do we know

14:04.886 --> 14:07.138
it's gonna end any differently
than it did before?

14:07.306 --> 14:08.931
Because before
you didn't have me.

14:09.808 --> 14:10.975
Hey, new girl?

14:11.143 --> 14:13.853
Everybody in this room
is about that superhero life.

14:14.646 --> 14:15.646
And if you don't mind
my asking,

14:15.731 --> 14:16.856
where the hell have you been
all this time?

14:16.940 --> 14:19.233
There are a lot of
other planets in the universe.

14:19.401 --> 14:22.278
And unfortunately,
they didn't have you guys.

14:32.456 --> 14:33.623
(RUMBLING)

14:41.923 --> 14:44.008
I like this one.

14:48.555 --> 14:51.015
Let's go get
this son of a bitch.

15:12.788 --> 15:13.788
Okay.

15:14.206 --> 15:16.582
Who here hasn't been to space?

15:17.959 --> 15:19.168
- Why?
- (CAROL CHUCKLES)

15:19.252 --> 15:20.920
You better not throw up
on my ship.

15:21.088 --> 15:22.380
Approaching jump in three...

15:22.798 --> 15:24.632
two, one.

15:38.188 --> 15:39.897
(OVER SPEAKERS)
<i>I'll head down for recon.</i>

15:58.417 --> 15:59.625
This is gonna work, Steve.

16:00.001 --> 16:01.585
I know it will.

16:05.424 --> 16:07.717
'Cause I don't know what
I'm gonna do if it doesn't.

16:08.301 --> 16:11.804
<i>No satellites.</i>
<i>No ships. No armies.</i>

16:11.972 --> 16:13.472
<i>No ground defenses</i>
<i>of any kind.</i>

16:15.559 --> 16:17.226
<i>It's just him.</i>

16:17.853 --> 16:19.603
And that's enough.

16:23.483 --> 16:25.401
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

17:06.860 --> 17:08.736
(POT CLANKING)

17:15.911 --> 17:16.911
(GRUNTS)

17:21.958 --> 17:23.083
(CHOKING)

17:23.460 --> 17:24.710
(GRUNTING)

17:33.261 --> 17:35.971
(SCREAMING)

17:37.557 --> 17:39.767
(THANOS GROANING)

17:48.652 --> 17:49.860
Oh, no.

17:57.869 --> 17:58.953
(GROANS)

17:59.746 --> 18:01.080
Where are they?

18:01.331 --> 18:03.082
- (GROANING)
- Answer the question.

18:05.544 --> 18:07.962
The universe
required correction.

18:08.129 --> 18:11.924
After that, the stones
served no purpose...

18:12.092 --> 18:13.717
beyond temptation.

18:13.885 --> 18:15.845
You murdered trillions!

18:16.805 --> 18:19.098
- You should be grateful.
- (BANNER GRUNTS)

18:22.602 --> 18:24.520
Where are the stones?

18:24.688 --> 18:26.063
Gone.

18:26.231 --> 18:27.314
Reduced to atoms.

18:27.983 --> 18:29.483
You used them two days ago!

18:29.651 --> 18:32.862
I used the stones
to destroy the stones.

18:33.613 --> 18:35.239
It nearly killed me.

18:36.658 --> 18:38.409
But the work is done.

18:38.827 --> 18:41.495
It always will be.

18:43.081 --> 18:46.458
I am inevitable.

18:48.753 --> 18:51.130
We have to tear this place
apart. He has to be lying!

18:51.298 --> 18:52.506
NEBULA: My father
is many things.

18:53.383 --> 18:55.467
A liar is not one of them.

18:57.512 --> 18:58.679
Ah.

18:59.472 --> 19:00.806
Thank you, daughter.

19:03.685 --> 19:05.603
Perhaps I treated you
too harshly.

19:05.937 --> 19:06.937
(GRUNTS)

19:12.110 --> 19:13.110
BANNER: What?

19:13.778 --> 19:15.529
What did you do?

19:17.073 --> 19:18.866
I went for the head.

20:29.771 --> 20:31.939
MAN: So...

20:33.274 --> 20:35.734
...I, uh, went on a date
the other day.

20:35.902 --> 20:37.569
It's the first time
in five years.

20:37.737 --> 20:40.072
You know?
I'm sitting there at dinner.

20:41.282 --> 20:43.283
I didn't even know
what to talk about.

20:44.619 --> 20:45.828
What did you talk about?

20:46.329 --> 20:49.665
Eh, same old crap. You know,
how things have changed.

20:50.291 --> 20:51.917
My job, his job.

20:52.919 --> 20:54.795
How much we miss the Mets.

20:57.215 --> 20:58.757
And then things got quiet...

21:00.969 --> 21:04.471
then he cried as they were
serving the salads.

21:04.639 --> 21:06.140
What about you?

21:07.225 --> 21:10.477
I cried just before dessert.

21:14.232 --> 21:16.358
But I'm seeing him
again tomorrow, so...

21:17.027 --> 21:18.277
That's great.

21:18.445 --> 21:20.112
You did the hardest part.
You took the jump.

21:20.196 --> 21:22.322
You didn't know where you
were gonna come down.

21:22.949 --> 21:24.825
And that's it.
That's those little

21:24.909 --> 21:27.244
brave baby steps
we gotta take...

21:27.412 --> 21:31.123
to try and become whole again,
try and find purpose.

21:32.959 --> 21:34.501
I went in the ice in '45,

21:34.586 --> 21:36.962
right after I met
the love of my life.

21:37.839 --> 21:39.590
Woke up 70 years later.

21:42.719 --> 21:44.762
You gotta move on.

21:47.474 --> 21:49.099
Gotta move on.

21:53.938 --> 21:56.356
The world is in our hands.

21:56.524 --> 21:58.609
It's left to us, guys.

21:58.777 --> 22:00.986
And we gotta do
something with it.

22:01.696 --> 22:03.113
Otherwise...

22:04.407 --> 22:06.742
Thanos should've killed
all of us.

22:30.016 --> 22:31.475
(RAT SQUEAKING)

22:39.734 --> 22:41.026
(BEEPS)

22:43.404 --> 22:44.988
(BEEPING)

22:45.073 --> 22:46.990
(POWERING UP)

22:54.082 --> 22:55.374
(GROANS)

23:02.590 --> 23:03.590
(BLOWS)

23:08.680 --> 23:10.013
What the hell?

23:11.891 --> 23:13.475
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

23:15.186 --> 23:16.395
(POWERS DOWN)

23:22.277 --> 23:23.652
Hope?

23:33.288 --> 23:34.913
(INAUDIBLE)

23:56.853 --> 23:57.853
Kid!

23:58.021 --> 23:59.062
Hey, kid!

24:03.401 --> 24:05.611
What the hell happened here?

24:17.540 --> 24:19.291
(BIRD CAWING)

24:37.268 --> 24:39.061
Oh, my God!

24:41.898 --> 24:43.357
Oh, please!

24:43.524 --> 24:45.067
Please, please!

24:45.235 --> 24:47.236
No, no, no. No.

24:48.696 --> 24:50.072
No.

24:52.408 --> 24:53.408
Excuse me. Sorry.

24:53.576 --> 24:54.868
Oh, Cassie, no.

24:55.036 --> 24:56.495
No, no, no.

24:57.872 --> 24:59.581
No, no.

25:00.500 --> 25:03.418
Please, please, please.
No, Cassie.

25:10.635 --> 25:11.802
What?

25:36.119 --> 25:37.911
(GASPING)

25:41.874 --> 25:43.208
Cassie?

25:44.377 --> 25:45.752
Dad?

25:48.798 --> 25:50.590
(CASSIE SOBBING)

26:01.978 --> 26:03.145
(SOBS)

26:11.779 --> 26:14.197
- You're so big!
- (BOTH LAUGH)

26:27.503 --> 26:28.795
ROCKET: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>Yeah. We boarded</i>

26:28.880 --> 26:32.007
<i>that highly-suspect warship</i>
<i>Danvers pinged.</i>

26:32.175 --> 26:33.884
<i>It was an infectious</i>
<i>garbage scow.</i>

26:34.052 --> 26:35.510
<i>So, thanks for the hot tip.</i>

26:35.678 --> 26:37.012
<i>Well, you were closer.</i>

26:37.180 --> 26:38.555
ROCKET: Yeah. And now
<i>we smell like garbage.</i>

26:38.639 --> 26:39.973
You get a reading
on those tremors?

26:40.141 --> 26:42.726
<i>'Twas a mild subduction</i>
<i>under the African plate.</i>

26:42.894 --> 26:44.936
Do we have a visual?
How are we handling it?

26:45.104 --> 26:46.271
OKOYE: Nat.

26:46.731 --> 26:48.690
<i>It's an earthquake</i>
<i>under the ocean.</i>

26:48.858 --> 26:51.693
<i>We handle it</i>
<i>by not handling it.</i>

26:52.445 --> 26:54.571
Carol, are we seeing you here
next month?

26:55.031 --> 26:56.114
<i>Not likely.</i>

26:56.199 --> 26:57.741
<i>What? You gonna get</i>
<i>another haircut?</i>

26:57.909 --> 26:59.242
<i>Listen, fur face.</i>

26:59.410 --> 27:01.203
<i>I'm covering</i>
<i>a lot of territory.</i>

27:01.371 --> 27:03.163
<i>The things</i>
<i>that are happening on Earth</i>

27:03.247 --> 27:04.498
<i>are happening everywhere.</i>

27:04.832 --> 27:06.666
<i>On thousands of planets.</i>

27:06.834 --> 27:08.335
<i>All right, all right.</i>
<i>That's a good point.</i>

27:08.419 --> 27:09.503
<i>That's a good point.</i>

27:09.670 --> 27:11.755
<i>So, you might not see me</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

27:12.590 --> 27:14.257
All right. Uh, well...

27:15.134 --> 27:17.260
This channel's always active.

27:17.428 --> 27:19.513
So, if anything
goes sideways...

27:19.680 --> 27:22.099
anyone's making trouble
where they shouldn't...

27:22.266 --> 27:23.433
comes through me.

27:23.518 --> 27:25.143
- (ASSENTS IN XHOSA)
<i>- Okay.</i>

27:25.228 --> 27:26.686
All right.

27:27.438 --> 27:28.522
<i>Good luck.</i>

27:33.361 --> 27:34.694
(SIGHS SOFTLY)

27:37.115 --> 27:38.115
Where are you?

27:38.282 --> 27:39.282
RHODES: Mexico.

27:39.450 --> 27:42.077
<i>The Federales found a room</i>
<i>full of bodies.</i>

27:42.245 --> 27:43.870
<i>Looks like</i>
<i>a bunch of cartel guys...</i>

27:44.038 --> 27:45.997
<i>never even had a chance</i>
<i>to get their guns off.</i>

27:46.165 --> 27:47.874
It's probably a rival gang.

27:48.042 --> 27:49.251
<i>Except it isn't.</i>

27:49.502 --> 27:51.586
<i>It's definitely Barton.</i>

27:52.171 --> 27:53.755
<i>What he's done here...</i>

27:53.923 --> 27:57.092
<i>what he's been doing</i>
<i>for the last few years...</i>

27:57.927 --> 27:59.719
<i>I mean,</i>
<i>the scene that he left...</i>

28:00.721 --> 28:01.721
<i>I gotta tell you,</i>

28:01.806 --> 28:04.266
<i>there's a part of me that</i>
<i>doesn't even wanna find him.</i>

28:09.856 --> 28:12.107
Will you find out
where he's going next?

28:16.028 --> 28:17.154
<i>Nat?</i>

28:18.948 --> 28:20.657
Please?

28:22.410 --> 28:23.577
<i>Okay.</i>

28:28.833 --> 28:30.459
(BREATHES SHAKILY)

28:32.378 --> 28:34.212
STEVE: You know, I'd offer
to cook you dinner...

28:34.547 --> 28:36.131
but you seem
pretty miserable already.

28:40.219 --> 28:41.636
NATASHA: You here
to do your laundry?

28:41.804 --> 28:43.388
And to see a friend.

28:44.474 --> 28:47.142
Clearly, your friend is fine.

28:49.896 --> 28:51.188
You know,
I saw a pod of whales

28:51.272 --> 28:52.397
when I was coming over
the bridge.

28:52.565 --> 28:54.399
- In the Hudson?
- There's fewer ships...

28:54.567 --> 28:55.817
cleaner water.

28:55.985 --> 28:57.861
You know,
if you're about to tell me

28:57.945 --> 28:59.905
to look on the bright side...

29:00.114 --> 29:01.323
Um...

29:02.283 --> 29:03.658
I'm about to hit you
in the head

29:03.743 --> 29:05.869
with a peanut butter sandwich.

29:05.953 --> 29:06.953
Hmm.

29:07.830 --> 29:08.997
Sorry.

29:09.165 --> 29:10.332
Force of habit.

29:24.597 --> 29:26.014
You know,
I keep telling everybody

29:26.098 --> 29:27.724
they should move on...

29:28.059 --> 29:29.559
and grow.

29:30.770 --> 29:32.062
Some do.

29:35.525 --> 29:37.025
But not us.

29:37.902 --> 29:39.819
If I move on, who does this?

29:40.196 --> 29:42.322
Maybe it doesn't need
to be done.

29:46.536 --> 29:48.787
I used to have nothing.

29:49.956 --> 29:51.873
And then I got this.

29:54.043 --> 29:55.877
This job.

29:58.256 --> 30:00.006
This family.

30:05.805 --> 30:07.681
And I was better
because of it.

30:13.938 --> 30:17.482
And even though
they're gone...

30:21.445 --> 30:23.863
I'm still trying to be better.

30:26.909 --> 30:29.327
I think we both need
to get a life.

30:31.872 --> 30:33.164
You first.

30:36.043 --> 30:37.460
(DEVICE CHIMES)

30:38.504 --> 30:39.879
SCOTT: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>Oh, hi, hi!</i>

30:39.964 --> 30:41.172
<i>Uh, is anyone home?</i>

30:41.340 --> 30:43.049
<i>This is, uh, Scott Lang.</i>

30:43.217 --> 30:46.052
<i>We met a few years ago</i>
<i>at the airport...</i>

30:46.220 --> 30:47.887
<i>in Germany?</i>

30:48.055 --> 30:50.348
<i>I was the guy that got</i>
<i>really big. I had a mask on.</i>

30:50.516 --> 30:52.100
<i>- You wouldn't recognize me.</i>
- Is this an old message?

30:52.184 --> 30:55.145
SCOTT: Ant-Man?
<i>I know you know that.</i>

30:55.313 --> 30:56.396
It's the front gate.

30:56.480 --> 30:57.897
<i>SCOTT: I really need</i>
<i>to talk to you guys.</i>

30:57.982 --> 31:00.150
(MUTTERING TO HIMSELF)

31:04.071 --> 31:05.238
STEVE: Scott.

31:06.198 --> 31:07.198
Are you okay?

31:07.366 --> 31:08.366
Yeah.

31:10.161 --> 31:12.537
Have either of you guys
ever studied quantum physics?

31:12.955 --> 31:14.456
Only to make conversation.

31:15.541 --> 31:17.167
All right, so...

31:17.543 --> 31:20.253
five years ago,
right before...

31:20.838 --> 31:21.963
Thanos...

31:22.340 --> 31:24.424
I was in a place
called the quantum realm.

31:24.592 --> 31:27.093
The quantum realm is like
its own microscopic universe.

31:27.511 --> 31:29.387
To get in there, you have
to be incredibly small.

31:29.555 --> 31:31.097
Hope. She's my, um...

31:33.184 --> 31:34.893
She was my...

31:36.604 --> 31:37.812
She was supposed to
pull me out.

31:37.980 --> 31:39.564
And then Thanos happened...

31:39.732 --> 31:41.399
and I got stuck in there.

31:41.859 --> 31:43.818
I'm sorry, that must have been
a very long five years.

31:43.986 --> 31:45.320
Yeah, but that's just it.

31:45.488 --> 31:46.655
It wasn't.

31:46.822 --> 31:48.031
For me, it was five hours.

31:48.199 --> 31:49.532
See, the rules of
the quantum realm

31:49.617 --> 31:50.700
aren't like they are up here.

31:50.785 --> 31:52.327
Everything is unpredictable.

31:52.495 --> 31:53.703
Is that anybody's sandwich?

31:53.871 --> 31:55.121
I'm starving.

31:55.456 --> 31:56.581
Scott.

31:56.749 --> 31:58.041
What are you talking about?

31:59.043 --> 32:00.293
(MUFFLED) So...

32:01.253 --> 32:02.837
what I'm saying is...

32:03.714 --> 32:06.132
time works differently
in the quantum realm.

32:06.300 --> 32:08.176
The only problem is right now

32:08.260 --> 32:09.678
we don't have a way
to navigate it.

32:09.762 --> 32:10.762
But what if we did?

32:11.514 --> 32:12.722
I can't stop thinking
about it.

32:12.807 --> 32:14.808
What if we could
somehow control the chaos...

32:14.892 --> 32:16.101
and we could navigate it?

32:16.185 --> 32:17.769
What if there was a way...

32:17.853 --> 32:19.479
that we could enter
the quantum realm

32:19.563 --> 32:20.647
at a certain point in time...

32:20.815 --> 32:22.273
but then exit
the quantum realm

32:22.358 --> 32:23.525
at another point in time?

32:23.693 --> 32:25.026
Like...

32:25.778 --> 32:27.862
- Like before Thanos.
- STEVE: Wait.

32:28.030 --> 32:29.614
Are you talking
about a time machine?

32:29.782 --> 32:32.534
No. No, of course not.
No, not a time machine.

32:32.702 --> 32:33.743
This is more like a...

32:36.080 --> 32:37.706
Yeah. Like a time machine.

32:37.873 --> 32:39.666
I know, it's crazy.
It's crazy.

32:39.750 --> 32:41.876
(STAMMERS) But I can't stop
thinking about it.

32:41.961 --> 32:43.211
There's gotta be...

32:43.963 --> 32:45.338
some way... (SIGHS)

32:45.423 --> 32:47.215
- It's crazy.
- NATASHA: Scott.

32:47.383 --> 32:48.675
I get emails from a raccoon...

32:48.843 --> 32:50.844
so nothing
sounds crazy anymore.

32:51.595 --> 32:53.680
So, who do we talk to
about this?

33:11.949 --> 33:13.032
Chow time!

33:15.494 --> 33:16.536
Maguna.

33:20.833 --> 33:22.208
Morgan H. Stark,
you want some lunch?

33:23.252 --> 33:24.252
<i>Define "lunch"</i>

33:24.336 --> 33:25.587
<i>- or be disintegrated.</i>
- Okay.

33:26.964 --> 33:28.465
You should not be
wearing that, okay?

33:28.591 --> 33:29.966
That is part of
a special anniversary gift

33:30.050 --> 33:31.134
I'm making for Mom.

33:34.889 --> 33:37.474
There you go.
You thinking about lunch?

33:37.641 --> 33:39.559
I can give you a handful of
crickets on a bed of lettuce.

33:39.727 --> 33:41.436
- No.
- That's what you want.

33:41.604 --> 33:43.730
How did you find this?

33:43.898 --> 33:45.732
- Garage.
- Really?

33:45.900 --> 33:47.901
- Were you looking for it?
- No.

33:48.778 --> 33:50.653
- I found it, though.
- Hmm.

33:50.821 --> 33:52.572
You like
going in the garage, huh?

33:52.740 --> 33:54.657
So does Daddy. (GRUNTS)

33:54.742 --> 33:57.577
It's fine, actually. Mom never
wears anything I buy her.

34:00.289 --> 34:01.539
So, I'm gonna...

34:19.058 --> 34:21.601
(STAMMERS) No.
We know what it sounds like.

34:21.685 --> 34:22.727
Tony, after everything
you've seen,

34:22.812 --> 34:23.812
is anything really impossible?

34:23.896 --> 34:26.105
Quantum fluctuation messes
with the Planck scale...

34:26.273 --> 34:27.941
which then triggers
the Deutsch Proposition.

34:28.025 --> 34:29.067
Can we agree on that?

34:29.235 --> 34:30.318
Thank you.

34:30.486 --> 34:32.612
In layman's terms, it means
you're not coming home.

34:32.947 --> 34:34.197
- I did.
- No.

34:34.365 --> 34:36.241
You accidentally survived.
(SIGHS)

34:36.325 --> 34:38.493
It's a billion-to-one
cosmic fluke.

34:38.661 --> 34:41.746
And now you wanna pull a...
What do you call it?

34:43.791 --> 34:45.124
A time heist?

34:45.292 --> 34:47.418
Yeah, a time heist. Of course.

34:47.503 --> 34:48.711
Why didn't we think
of this before?

34:48.796 --> 34:51.339
Oh, because it's laughable.
Because it's a pipe dream.

34:51.423 --> 34:53.591
The stones are in the past.

34:53.676 --> 34:55.009
We could go back,
we could get them.

34:55.177 --> 34:57.470
We can snap our own fingers.
We can bring everybody back.

34:57.638 --> 34:59.556
Or screw it up worse than
he already has, right?

34:59.723 --> 35:00.723
I don't believe we would.

35:01.308 --> 35:03.852
Gotta say it. I sometimes miss
that giddy optimism.

35:04.728 --> 35:06.437
However, high hopes
won't help...

35:06.605 --> 35:08.565
if there's no logical,
tangible way

35:08.649 --> 35:12.110
for me to safely execute
said time heist.

35:12.278 --> 35:14.153
I believe
the most likely outcome

35:14.238 --> 35:15.238
will be our collective demise.

35:15.322 --> 35:18.157
Not if we strictly follow
the rules of time travel.

35:18.325 --> 35:20.994
All right? It means no talking
to our past selves...

35:21.078 --> 35:22.620
no betting on sporting events.

35:22.788 --> 35:24.539
I'm gonna stop you
right there, Scott.

35:25.457 --> 35:26.833
Are you seriously telling me

35:26.917 --> 35:28.710
that your plan
to save the universe...

35:28.878 --> 35:30.545
is based on
<i>Back to the Future?</i>

35:31.672 --> 35:33.423
- Is it?
- No.

35:33.591 --> 35:34.632
Good. You had me
worried there.

35:34.717 --> 35:35.758
'Cause that would be
horseshit.

35:35.926 --> 35:38.219
That's not how
quantum physics works.

35:38.387 --> 35:39.554
Tony.

35:41.515 --> 35:42.974
We have to take a stand.

35:43.642 --> 35:45.518
We did stand.
And yet, here we are.

35:47.855 --> 35:49.147
SCOTT: I know you got
a lot on the line.

35:49.648 --> 35:52.191
You got a wife, a daughter.

35:52.359 --> 35:54.861
But I lost someone
very important to me.

35:55.029 --> 35:56.613
A lotta people did.

35:56.780 --> 35:59.782
And now, now we have a chance
to bring her back...

35:59.950 --> 36:01.117
to bring everyone back,

36:01.201 --> 36:02.702
and you're telling me
that you won't even...

36:02.786 --> 36:04.579
That's right, Scott.
I won't even.

36:06.290 --> 36:07.624
- I can't.
- (DOOR CLOSES)

36:07.708 --> 36:09.042
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

36:09.793 --> 36:12.128
MORGAN STARK: Mommy told me
to come and save you.

36:12.212 --> 36:14.631
Good job. I'm saved.

36:15.382 --> 36:17.425
I wish you were coming here
to ask me something else.

36:17.509 --> 36:18.635
Anything else.

36:18.719 --> 36:20.511
I'm honestly happy
to see you guys, I just...

36:20.596 --> 36:21.971
Oh, look,
the table's set for six.

36:22.056 --> 36:23.556
Tony. I get it.

36:23.724 --> 36:26.017
And I'm happy for you.
I really am.

36:26.810 --> 36:28.311
But this is a second chance.

36:29.021 --> 36:31.439
I got my second chance
right here, Cap.

36:31.607 --> 36:33.149
Can't roll the dice on it.

36:35.235 --> 36:37.153
If you don't talk shop,
you can stay for lunch.

36:40.407 --> 36:41.616
Well, he's scared.

36:42.284 --> 36:43.409
STEVE: He's not wrong.

36:43.494 --> 36:45.578
SCOTT: Yeah, but, I mean,
what are we gonna do?

36:45.663 --> 36:46.955
We need him.
What, are we gonna stop?

36:47.873 --> 36:49.874
No, I wanna do it right.

36:53.087 --> 36:54.754
We're gonna need
a really big brain.

36:55.839 --> 36:57.006
Bigger than his?

36:57.716 --> 36:59.300
Come on, I feel like
I'm the only one eating here.

36:59.385 --> 37:00.426
Try some of that.

37:00.511 --> 37:01.511
Have some eggs.

37:02.012 --> 37:03.346
I'm so confused.

37:03.430 --> 37:05.181
These are confusing times.
(CHUCKLES)

37:05.265 --> 37:07.183
Right, no, no.
That's not what I meant.

37:07.351 --> 37:09.852
Nah, I get it. I'm kidding!

37:10.437 --> 37:12.230
I know, it's crazy.

37:12.398 --> 37:13.606
I'm wearing shirts now.

37:13.774 --> 37:16.609
Yeah. What? How? Why?

37:17.069 --> 37:19.404
Five years ago,
we got our asses beat.

37:20.030 --> 37:21.656
Except it was worse for me...

37:21.824 --> 37:23.032
'cause I lost twice.

37:23.200 --> 37:24.993
First, Hulk lost,
then Banner lost...

37:25.869 --> 37:27.203
and then, we all lost.

37:27.287 --> 37:28.538
No one blamed you, Bruce.

37:28.706 --> 37:30.081
I did.

37:31.834 --> 37:33.084
For years,
I've been treating the Hulk

37:33.168 --> 37:34.293
like he's
some kind of disease...

37:34.378 --> 37:35.837
something to get rid of.

37:36.588 --> 37:39.257
But then, I start looking
at him as the cure.

37:39.842 --> 37:41.968
Eighteen months
in the gamma lab.

37:42.136 --> 37:44.721
I put the brains
and the brawn together...

37:44.888 --> 37:46.139
and now, look at me.

37:47.182 --> 37:48.516
Best of both worlds.

37:49.268 --> 37:50.601
- Excuse me, Mr. Hulk?
- Yes.

37:50.769 --> 37:52.103
Can we get a photo?

37:52.521 --> 37:54.522
100%, little person.

37:54.690 --> 37:56.733
Come on, step on up.
Do you mind?

37:57.443 --> 37:59.193
- Oh, yeah, yeah.
- SMART HULK: Thanks.

37:59.278 --> 38:00.862
Say "green."

38:01.030 --> 38:03.281
- FANS: Green.
- Green.

38:03.365 --> 38:04.365
Did you get that?

38:04.533 --> 38:05.783
That's a good one.

38:06.577 --> 38:08.828
Did you want to grab one
with me? I'm Ant-Man.

38:12.499 --> 38:14.417
They're Hulk fans.
They don't know Ant-Man.

38:14.501 --> 38:15.668
- Nobody does.
- No, he wants you to take

38:15.753 --> 38:17.462
- a picture with him.
- I don't want a picture.

38:17.546 --> 38:18.629
BOY 1: Stranger danger.

38:18.714 --> 38:20.256
Yeah, look, he's even
saying no, he doesn't.

38:20.340 --> 38:21.340
I get it.
I don't want it, either.

38:21.425 --> 38:22.550
But come on. The kid...

38:22.634 --> 38:24.052
I don't want a picture
with them.

38:24.219 --> 38:25.219
- He's gonna feel bad.
- Sorry.

38:25.304 --> 38:26.637
They're happy to do it.
They said they'll do it.

38:26.722 --> 38:28.264
SCOTT: I don't want to do it.
BOY 2: We can do it.

38:28.348 --> 38:30.391
- SMART HULK: No, you feel bad.
- Take the goddamn phone.

38:30.476 --> 38:31.684
SMART HULK: Okay.

38:31.769 --> 38:32.769
GIRL: Thank you, Mr. Hulk.

38:32.853 --> 38:34.520
SMART HULK: No, it was great,
kids. Thank you very much.

38:34.980 --> 38:36.355
ALL: Hulk out!

38:36.523 --> 38:37.565
STEVE: Bruce.

38:37.983 --> 38:38.983
Dab.

38:39.318 --> 38:40.943
- Bruce.
- Listen to your mom.

38:41.320 --> 38:42.320
She knows better.

38:42.488 --> 38:44.155
About what we were saying.

38:44.323 --> 38:45.531
Right.

38:47.493 --> 38:50.161
The whole time travel do-over?

38:51.455 --> 38:55.208
Eh, guys, it's outside of
my area of expertise.

38:55.667 --> 38:56.918
Well, you pulled this off.

38:57.961 --> 39:01.756
I remember a time when that
seemed pretty impossible, too.

39:35.040 --> 39:36.582
I've got a mild inspiration.

39:36.667 --> 39:37.959
I'd like to see
if it checks out.

39:38.043 --> 39:40.128
So, I'd like to run
one last sim

39:40.212 --> 39:41.796
before we pack it in
for the night.

39:41.964 --> 39:44.966
This time, in the shape
of a Mobius strip,

39:45.050 --> 39:46.425
inverted, please.

39:46.510 --> 39:47.593
<i>FRIDAY: Processing.</i>

39:51.056 --> 39:53.558
Right, give me the eigenvalue
of that particle...

39:53.725 --> 39:55.726
factoring in spectral decomp.

39:55.894 --> 39:57.854
- That'll take a second.
<i>- FRIDAY: Just a moment.</i>

39:58.897 --> 40:01.774
And don't worry if it doesn't
pan out. I'm just kinda...

40:03.318 --> 40:04.777
<i>Model rendered.</i>

40:04.862 --> 40:05.903
(PUFFS)

40:11.702 --> 40:13.369
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

40:16.623 --> 40:17.623
Shit!

40:17.958 --> 40:19.208
MORGAN STARK: Shit!

40:23.255 --> 40:24.964
(WHISPERS) What are you
doing up, little miss?

40:25.132 --> 40:26.841
- Shit.
- Nope. We don't say that.

40:27.009 --> 40:28.217
Only Mommy says that word.

40:28.385 --> 40:29.802
She coined it.
It belongs to her.

40:29.970 --> 40:30.970
Why are you up?

40:31.096 --> 40:32.471
'Cause I've got some
important shit going on here!

40:32.639 --> 40:33.806
Why do you think?

40:33.974 --> 40:35.516
No, I got something
on my mind.

40:35.601 --> 40:36.934
I got something on my mind.

40:37.102 --> 40:38.644
Was it juice pops?

40:40.189 --> 40:41.397
Sure was.

40:42.816 --> 40:44.567
That's extortion.
That's a word.

40:44.735 --> 40:45.902
What kind you want?

40:46.069 --> 40:47.069
Great minds think alike.

40:47.237 --> 40:49.071
Juice pops exactly...

40:51.241 --> 40:52.366
was on my mind.

40:53.785 --> 40:54.911
You done? Yeah?

40:55.454 --> 40:56.662
Now you are.

40:57.247 --> 40:58.414
Here. Wipe.

41:01.126 --> 41:03.794
Good. That face goes there.

41:03.962 --> 41:05.213
Tell me a story.

41:05.380 --> 41:06.964
A story.

41:07.132 --> 41:09.258
Once upon a time,
Maguna went to bed. The end.

41:09.635 --> 41:11.010
That is a horrible story.

41:11.178 --> 41:12.929
Come on,
that's your favorite story.

41:13.639 --> 41:14.805
Love you tons.

41:16.808 --> 41:18.643
I love you 3,000.

41:19.895 --> 41:20.895
Wow.

41:28.237 --> 41:31.113
(WHISPERS) 3,000.
That's crazy.

41:32.324 --> 41:34.116
Go to bed
or I'll sell all your toys.

41:35.327 --> 41:36.661
- Night night.
- (DOOR CLOSES)

41:36.828 --> 41:38.037
Not that it's a competition...

41:38.538 --> 41:40.456
but she loves me 3,000.

41:40.624 --> 41:41.707
Does she, now?

41:41.875 --> 41:44.919
You were somewhere in
the low 6 to 900 range.

41:45.003 --> 41:46.045
(CHUCKLES)

41:50.968 --> 41:52.468
Whatcha reading?

41:53.095 --> 41:54.553
Just a book on composting.

41:54.721 --> 41:56.806
What's new with composting?

41:58.267 --> 42:00.309
- Interesting science...
- I figured it out.

42:01.395 --> 42:02.395
By the way.

42:03.272 --> 42:04.438
And, you know,

42:04.523 --> 42:06.649
just so we're talking
about the same thing...

42:06.817 --> 42:08.276
Time travel.

42:08.777 --> 42:09.777
What?

42:13.991 --> 42:14.991
Wow.

42:19.079 --> 42:20.621
That's amazing...

42:21.581 --> 42:22.707
and terrifying.

42:22.874 --> 42:24.333
That's right.

42:28.547 --> 42:29.755
(PEPPER SIGHS)

42:31.633 --> 42:33.342
We got really lucky.

42:33.510 --> 42:34.510
Yeah.

42:34.678 --> 42:35.803
I know.

42:35.971 --> 42:37.096
A lot of people didn't.

42:37.264 --> 42:38.889
Nope. And I can't
help everybody.

42:40.642 --> 42:41.976
Sorta seems like you can.

42:42.144 --> 42:43.769
Not if I stop.

42:44.938 --> 42:47.815
I can put a pin in it
right now and stop.

42:48.608 --> 42:49.608
Tony...

42:50.319 --> 42:51.861
trying to get you to stop...

42:52.029 --> 42:54.655
has been one of the few
failures of my entire life.

42:58.952 --> 43:00.619
Something tells me...

43:01.913 --> 43:02.997
I should put it in a lockbox

43:03.081 --> 43:04.582
and drop it
to the bottom of the lake...

43:05.792 --> 43:07.001
and go to bed.

43:13.383 --> 43:15.426
But would you be able to rest?

43:20.891 --> 43:23.476
SMART HULK: Okay, here we go.
Time travel test number one.

43:23.643 --> 43:25.811
Scott, fire up...

43:26.730 --> 43:27.897
the, uh, van thing.

43:30.192 --> 43:31.233
STEVE: Breakers are set.

43:31.401 --> 43:33.235
Emergency generators
are on standby.

43:33.403 --> 43:35.112
Good, because
if we blow the grid,

43:35.197 --> 43:38.407
I don't want to lose, uh,
Tiny here in the 1950s.

43:38.492 --> 43:41.452
- Excuse me?
- He's kidding.

43:41.620 --> 43:43.496
You can't say things
like that.

43:43.580 --> 43:45.247
(STAMMERS)
It was a bad joke.

43:47.250 --> 43:48.250
You were kidding, right?

43:48.377 --> 43:51.504
I have no idea. We're talking
about time travel here.

43:51.671 --> 43:53.923
Either it's all a joke,
or none of it is.

43:54.091 --> 43:55.758
We're good!

43:55.926 --> 43:57.259
Get your helmet on.

43:57.886 --> 43:59.762
Scott, I'm gonna
send you back a week...

43:59.846 --> 44:01.472
let you walk around
for an hour,

44:01.556 --> 44:03.057
then bring you back
in 10 seconds.

44:03.225 --> 44:04.225
Make sense?

44:04.893 --> 44:06.143
Perfectly not confusing.

44:06.311 --> 44:08.270
Good luck, Scott.
You got this.

44:09.815 --> 44:12.858
You're right.
I do, Captain America.

44:15.028 --> 44:16.362
On a count of three...

44:16.530 --> 44:20.408
Three, two, one.

44:20.492 --> 44:21.992
(MACHINE WHIRS)

44:23.662 --> 44:25.329
Uh... Guys?

44:25.789 --> 44:27.373
This doesn't feel right.

44:27.457 --> 44:28.457
STEVE: What is this?

44:28.542 --> 44:29.542
- What's going on?
- NATASHA: Who is that?

44:29.626 --> 44:30.626
- Hold on.
- Is that Scott?

44:30.710 --> 44:31.710
Yes, it's Scott.

44:34.589 --> 44:37.216
- What's going on, Bruce?
- Oh, my back!

44:37.300 --> 44:38.300
- What is this?
- Hold on a second.

44:38.385 --> 44:39.385
Could I get
a little space here?

44:39.469 --> 44:40.594
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Can you bring him back?

44:40.679 --> 44:41.720
I'm working on it.

44:41.805 --> 44:43.139
(BEEPING)

44:48.770 --> 44:49.770
It's a baby.

44:49.938 --> 44:51.480
- It's Scott.
- STEVE: As a baby.

44:51.648 --> 44:53.107
- SMART HULK: He'll grow.
- Bring Scott back.

44:53.191 --> 44:54.650
When I say kill the power,
kill the power.

44:54.734 --> 44:55.985
Oh, my God.

44:56.695 --> 44:58.070
And... kill it!

45:02.492 --> 45:04.285
Somebody peed my pants.

45:04.369 --> 45:05.411
Oh, thank God.

45:05.579 --> 45:08.789
But I don't know
if it was baby me or old me.

45:12.127 --> 45:14.086
Or just me me.

45:14.504 --> 45:15.713
Time travel!

45:19.468 --> 45:20.468
What?

45:22.137 --> 45:24.388
I see this as an absolute win.

45:38.445 --> 45:41.030
- (TIRES SQUEALING)
- (ENGINE ROARING)

46:10.060 --> 46:11.352
Why the long face?

46:11.520 --> 46:13.270
Let me guess,
he turned into a baby.

46:14.523 --> 46:16.524
Among other things, yeah.
What are you doing here?

46:16.691 --> 46:18.108
It's the EPR Paradox.

46:18.902 --> 46:19.902
Instead of pushing Lang
through time,

46:19.986 --> 46:20.986
you might've wound up...

46:21.112 --> 46:22.530
pushing time through Lang.

46:22.697 --> 46:23.822
It's tricky, dangerous.

46:23.907 --> 46:25.366
Somebody could have
cautioned you against it.

46:25.534 --> 46:26.534
You did.

46:26.660 --> 46:27.868
Oh, did I?

46:28.036 --> 46:29.703
Well, thank God I'm here.

46:30.497 --> 46:32.122
Regardless, I fixed it.

46:33.208 --> 46:35.501
A fully functioning
time-space GPS.

46:37.587 --> 46:38.837
I just want peace.

46:40.465 --> 46:43.175
Turns out resentment
is corrosive, and I hate it.

46:44.052 --> 46:45.427
Me, too.

46:46.680 --> 46:48.138
We got a shot
at getting these stones,

46:48.223 --> 46:50.140
but I gotta tell you
my priorities.

46:50.308 --> 46:52.643
Bring back what we lost,
I hope, yes.

46:52.811 --> 46:55.646
Keep what I found,
I have to, at all costs.

46:56.898 --> 46:59.483
And maybe not die trying.

46:59.651 --> 47:00.693
Would be nice.

47:03.154 --> 47:04.238
Sounds like a deal.

47:24.467 --> 47:25.801
(SIGHS)

47:27.846 --> 47:28.846
Tony, I don't know.

47:29.014 --> 47:30.639
Why?

47:30.807 --> 47:32.600
He made it for you.

47:32.767 --> 47:34.518
Plus, honestly, I have to
get it out of the garage

47:34.603 --> 47:36.353
before Morgan
takes it sledding.

47:41.901 --> 47:43.027
Thank you, Tony.

47:44.029 --> 47:45.571
Will you keep that
a little quiet?

47:46.281 --> 47:47.656
Didn't bring one
for the whole team.

47:49.409 --> 47:52.703
We are getting
the whole team, yeah?

47:52.871 --> 47:54.622
We're working on that
right now.

48:03.923 --> 48:06.050
(SPACESHIP ENGINE HUMMING)

48:12.724 --> 48:13.766
ROCKET: Hey, Humie.

48:14.309 --> 48:16.101
Where's Big Green?

48:16.436 --> 48:18.479
The kitchen, I think.

48:19.731 --> 48:20.939
That's awesome.

48:22.150 --> 48:24.234
Rhodey, careful on re-entry.

48:24.402 --> 48:26.111
There's an idiot
in the landing zone.

48:27.280 --> 48:28.405
Oh, God.

48:28.990 --> 48:31.033
WAR MACHINE: What's up,
<i>Regular-Sized Man?</i>

48:35.413 --> 48:37.456
(CALYPSO ROCK SONG PLAYING)

49:21.876 --> 49:24.336
ROCKET: Kind of a step down
from the golden palaces

49:24.421 --> 49:26.171
and the magic hammers
and whatnot.

49:26.297 --> 49:27.673
Hey, have
a little compassion, pal.

49:27.841 --> 49:29.800
First, they lost Asgard,
then half their people.

49:29.968 --> 49:31.510
They're probably just happy
to have a home.

49:31.678 --> 49:33.387
You shouldn't have come.

49:33.471 --> 49:35.055
Ah!

49:35.473 --> 49:36.473
Valkyrie!

49:36.641 --> 49:39.351
Great to see you, angry girl!

49:39.519 --> 49:41.729
I think I liked you better
either of the other ways.

49:42.981 --> 49:44.773
- This is Rocket.
- How ya doing?

49:47.193 --> 49:48.193
He won't see you.

49:48.528 --> 49:49.570
It's that bad, huh?

49:49.738 --> 49:51.155
We only see him once a month

49:51.239 --> 49:54.366
when he comes
in for "supplies."

49:55.452 --> 49:56.577
It's that bad.

49:56.745 --> 49:57.745
Yeah.

50:03.293 --> 50:04.752
(DOOR CREAKS)

50:10.258 --> 50:11.300
What the...?

50:11.384 --> 50:12.968
- (SNIFFS)
- (FLOORBOARD CREAKING)

50:13.803 --> 50:16.388
Whew! Something died in here!

50:16.473 --> 50:19.767
- (BOTTLES CLINK)
- SMART HULK: Hello? Thor!

50:20.310 --> 50:21.977
THOR: Are you here
about the cable?

50:22.729 --> 50:24.813
The Cinemax went out
two weeks ago...

50:25.398 --> 50:28.150
and the sports are all
kinda fuzzy and whatnot.

50:28.902 --> 50:29.902
SMART HULK: Thor?

50:37.827 --> 50:40.412
(LAUGHING) Boys! Oh, my God!

50:41.039 --> 50:43.791
Oh, my God,
it's so good to see you!

50:45.251 --> 50:46.543
Come here,
cuddly little rascal.

50:46.711 --> 50:49.213
- Yeah, no, I'm good. I'm good.
- (THOR MOANS AND LAUGHS)

50:49.339 --> 50:50.422
That's not necessary.

50:50.882 --> 50:53.550
Hulk, you know my friends
Miek and Korg, right?

50:53.718 --> 50:54.843
- Hey, boys!
- SMART HULK: Hey, guys.

50:55.011 --> 50:56.261
Long time no see.

50:56.429 --> 50:57.429
Beer's in the bucket.

50:57.514 --> 50:58.680
Feel free to log on
to the Wi-Fi.

50:58.848 --> 51:00.557
No password, obviously.

51:01.643 --> 51:03.143
Thor, he's back.

51:03.311 --> 51:05.979
That kid on the TV just
called me a dickhead again.

51:06.523 --> 51:07.564
Noobmaster.

51:07.732 --> 51:10.192
KORG: Yeah, NoobMaster69
called me a dickhead.

51:10.360 --> 51:11.527
I am sick of this.

51:12.445 --> 51:14.112
Noobmaster, hey,
it's Thor again.

51:14.197 --> 51:15.364
You know, the God of Thunder.

51:15.532 --> 51:17.699
Listen, bud, if you don't log
off this game immediately...

51:17.867 --> 51:19.368
I am gonna fly over
to your house,

51:19.494 --> 51:20.994
come down to that basement
you're hiding in...

51:21.162 --> 51:23.789
rip off your arms,
and shove them up your butt!

51:24.165 --> 51:25.249
Oh, that's right, yes!

51:25.333 --> 51:27.209
Go cry to your father,
you little weasel.

51:27.919 --> 51:28.919
Thank you, Thor.

51:29.003 --> 51:30.420
Let me know if
he bothers you again, okay?

51:30.588 --> 51:31.797
Thank you very much. I will.

51:32.590 --> 51:34.174
So, you guys want a drink?
What are we drinking?

51:34.259 --> 51:36.677
I've got beer, tequila,
all sorts of things.

51:37.011 --> 51:38.220
(CHUCKLES)

51:39.556 --> 51:40.973
SMART HULK: Buddy.

51:41.140 --> 51:43.600
- You all right?
- Yes, I'm fine. Why?

51:43.768 --> 51:44.810
Why, don't I look all right?

51:45.228 --> 51:46.645
You look
like melted ice cream.

51:46.729 --> 51:48.021
(LAUGHS)

51:48.648 --> 51:50.732
So, what's up? You just here
for a hang, or what?

51:50.900 --> 51:53.026
- We need your help.
- Mm.

51:53.111 --> 51:55.404
There might be a chance
we could fix everything.

51:55.572 --> 51:56.905
What, like the cable?

51:56.990 --> 51:59.283
(BURPS) 'Cause that's been
driving me bananas for weeks.

51:59.450 --> 52:00.450
Like Thanos.

52:19.637 --> 52:22.472
Don't say that name.

52:23.266 --> 52:26.310
Um, yeah, we don't actually
say that name in here.

52:31.149 --> 52:33.025
SMART HULK: Please take
your hand off me.

52:36.446 --> 52:39.489
Now, I know that guy...

52:40.408 --> 52:41.533
might scare you.

52:41.701 --> 52:43.160
Why would I be...? (SCOFFS)

52:43.244 --> 52:46.413
Why would I be scared
of that guy?

52:46.581 --> 52:48.415
I'm the one
who killed that guy, remember?

52:48.499 --> 52:49.666
Hmm.

52:49.751 --> 52:51.627
Anyone else here
kill that guy?

52:55.048 --> 52:56.131
Nope.

52:56.674 --> 52:57.674
Didn't think so.

52:58.760 --> 53:00.594
Korg, why don't you, uh,
tell everybody

53:00.678 --> 53:03.013
who chopped
Thanos' big head off?

53:03.097 --> 53:04.598
Um, Stormbreaker?

53:04.766 --> 53:06.391
THOR: Who was swinging
Stormbreaker?

53:10.480 --> 53:12.689
I get it.
You're in a rough spot, okay?

53:12.857 --> 53:13.857
I've been there myself.

53:14.025 --> 53:16.318
And you want to know
who helped me out of it?

53:16.486 --> 53:18.820
(SLURRING) Was it Natasha?

53:19.280 --> 53:21.156
It was you.

53:21.324 --> 53:23.283
You helped me.

53:24.494 --> 53:25.953
So, why don't you ask...

53:27.038 --> 53:29.373
the Asgardians down there...

53:29.540 --> 53:31.249
how much my help is worth?

53:36.923 --> 53:38.382
The ones
that are left, anyway.

53:38.925 --> 53:40.509
I think we could
bring them back.

53:40.593 --> 53:42.427
(CHUCKLES) Stop.

53:43.554 --> 53:45.305
Stop, okay? (SNIFFS)

53:45.390 --> 53:46.598
I know you think I'm down here

53:46.683 --> 53:48.308
wallowing in my own
self-pity...

53:48.476 --> 53:51.019
waiting to be rescued
and saved...

53:51.187 --> 53:53.271
but I'm fine, okay.
We're fine, aren't we?

53:53.439 --> 53:54.898
Oh, we're good here, mate.

53:55.066 --> 53:57.025
So, whatever it is that you're
offering, we're not into it.

53:57.193 --> 53:58.694
Don't care.
Couldn't care less.

53:58.861 --> 53:59.945
Goodbye.

54:00.613 --> 54:01.863
(CHUCKLES)

54:03.324 --> 54:05.033
SMART HULK: We need you, pal.

54:06.494 --> 54:07.744
(SNIFFS)

54:08.830 --> 54:10.122
(CHUCKLES QUIETLY)

54:14.460 --> 54:16.461
There's beer on the ship.

54:19.173 --> 54:20.424
(BOTTLE CLATTERS)

54:20.508 --> 54:22.134
What kind?

54:29.392 --> 54:31.309
(MAN SHOUTS IN JAPANESE)

54:31.686 --> 54:33.645
- (GRUNTS)
- (GROANS)

54:34.147 --> 54:35.147
(MAN SHOUTS IN JAPANESE)

54:41.320 --> 54:42.320
(GROANS)

54:48.828 --> 54:50.495
(GUNFIRE)

54:59.213 --> 55:00.422
(GRUNTS)

55:20.651 --> 55:21.777
(GRUNTS)

55:28.076 --> 55:29.534
(SCOFFS)

55:34.165 --> 55:35.624
(BOTH GRUNTING)

55:52.391 --> 55:53.767
(SHOUTS IN JAPANESE)

55:53.851 --> 55:54.893
(YELLS)

55:55.770 --> 55:57.312
(GAGGING)

56:08.366 --> 56:11.451
(IN ENGLISH)
What I want you can't give me.

56:35.351 --> 56:36.518
You shouldn't be here.

56:39.230 --> 56:40.981
Neither should you.

56:46.988 --> 56:48.446
I've got a job to do.

56:50.032 --> 56:51.658
NATASHA: Is that what
you're calling this?

56:52.743 --> 56:55.162
Killing all these people isn't
gonna bring your family back.

57:01.002 --> 57:02.085
We found something.

57:03.754 --> 57:05.922
A chance, maybe.

57:08.009 --> 57:10.468
(SIGHS) Don't.

57:11.387 --> 57:12.846
Don't what?

57:15.892 --> 57:17.350
Don't give me hope.

57:20.688 --> 57:23.148
I'm sorry I couldn't
give it to you sooner.

57:37.038 --> 57:38.038
(ROCK AND ROLL SONG PLAYING)

57:44.712 --> 57:46.004
You're drifting left.

57:46.589 --> 57:48.298
One side there, Lebowski.

57:51.510 --> 57:52.802
Ratchet, how's it going?

57:52.970 --> 57:53.970
It's Rocket.

57:54.138 --> 57:56.681
Take it easy. You're only
a genius on Earth, pal.

57:56.807 --> 57:57.807
(THOR BELCHES)

58:01.604 --> 58:03.188
RHODES: Time travel suit,
not bad.

58:04.649 --> 58:06.149
Hey, hey, hey!
Easy! Easy!

58:06.234 --> 58:07.234
I'm being very careful.

58:07.401 --> 58:08.818
No, you're being very Hulky.

58:08.903 --> 58:09.903
I'm being careful.

58:10.071 --> 58:11.446
These are Pym Particles,
all right?

58:11.614 --> 58:12.864
And ever since
Hank Pym got snapped

58:12.949 --> 58:14.199
out of existence, this is it.

58:14.283 --> 58:16.034
This is what we have.
We're not making any more.

58:16.202 --> 58:18.119
- Scott, calm down.
- SCOTT: Sorry.

58:18.454 --> 58:21.414
We've got enough for one
round-trip each. That's it.

58:21.582 --> 58:22.624
No do-overs.

58:23.668 --> 58:25.001
Plus two test runs.

58:26.128 --> 58:27.504
- (SUIT FASTENING)
- (YELLS)

58:29.006 --> 58:30.006
One test run.

58:30.132 --> 58:31.258
(SIGHS)

58:31.342 --> 58:32.926
All right.
I'm not ready for this.

58:33.094 --> 58:34.386
BARTON: I'm game.

58:36.597 --> 58:38.348
I'll do it.

58:38.975 --> 58:40.141
SMART HULK:
Clint, now you're gonna feel

58:40.226 --> 58:41.726
a little discombobulated
from the chronoshift.

58:41.811 --> 58:42.811
Don't worry about that.

58:42.895 --> 58:44.020
RHODES: Wait a second.
Let me ask you something.

58:44.188 --> 58:45.814
If we can do this, you know...

58:45.982 --> 58:48.316
go back in time, why don't
we just find baby Thanos?

58:48.484 --> 58:49.651
You know, and...

58:53.239 --> 58:54.739
First of all, that's horrible.

58:54.824 --> 58:55.824
It's Thanos.

58:55.908 --> 58:57.993
And secondly,
time doesn't work that way.

58:58.160 --> 59:00.328
Changing the past
doesn't change the future.

59:00.496 --> 59:01.871
Look, we go back,
we get the stones

59:01.956 --> 59:03.206
before Thanos gets them...

59:03.374 --> 59:06.126
Thanos doesn't have
the stones. Problem solved.

59:06.294 --> 59:08.128
- Bingo.
- That's not how it works.

59:08.212 --> 59:09.212
Well, that's what I heard.

59:09.297 --> 59:10.422
Wait, but who?
Who told you that?

59:10.589 --> 59:12.382
<i>Star Trek,</i>
<i>Terminator, Timecop...</i>

59:12.550 --> 59:14.134
<i>- Time After Time.</i>
<i>- Quantum Leap.</i>

59:14.302 --> 59:15.343
<i>Wrinkle in Time,</i>
<i>Somewhere in Time.</i>

59:15.428 --> 59:16.428
<i>Hot Tub Time Machine.</i>

59:16.512 --> 59:17.554
<i>Hot Tub Time Machine.</i>

59:17.638 --> 59:18.888
<i>Bill and Ted's</i>
<i>Excellent Adventure.</i>

59:19.056 --> 59:21.141
Basically, any movie
that deals with time travel.

59:21.309 --> 59:23.143
<i>Die Hard.</i>
No, that's not one.

59:23.311 --> 59:24.352
This is known.

59:24.520 --> 59:25.729
I don't know
why everyone believes that,

59:25.813 --> 59:26.855
but that isn't true.

59:26.939 --> 59:28.940
Think about it.
If you travel to the past...

59:29.108 --> 59:31.443
that past becomes
your future...

59:31.610 --> 59:34.571
and your former present
becomes the past...

59:34.739 --> 59:37.365
which can't now be changed
by your new future.

59:37.533 --> 59:38.742
Exactly.

59:39.327 --> 59:42.203
<i>So Back to the Future</i>
is a bunch of bullshit?

59:46.125 --> 59:48.084
- All right, Clint.
- (BEEPING)

59:48.210 --> 59:51.254
We're going in three, two...

59:51.422 --> 59:52.422
one.

59:56.218 --> 59:57.385
(GRUNTS)

01:00:03.726 --> 01:00:05.435
(YELLING)

01:00:07.772 --> 01:00:09.022
(PANTING)

01:00:09.774 --> 01:00:10.815
(GASPS)

01:00:31.837 --> 01:00:33.671
(CONTINUES PANTING)

01:01:04.787 --> 01:01:06.121
LILA: Cooper?

01:01:06.288 --> 01:01:07.831
Where are my headphones?

01:01:07.915 --> 01:01:08.915
Lila?

01:01:09.083 --> 01:01:11.126
- COOPER: I never had them.
- Lila?

01:01:11.210 --> 01:01:12.210
(BEEPING)

01:01:12.294 --> 01:01:13.920
LILA: Yeah,
you had them yesterday!

01:01:14.505 --> 01:01:15.797
Lila! Lila!

01:01:21.303 --> 01:01:22.303
Yeah, Dad?

01:01:26.183 --> 01:01:27.225
Dad?

01:01:29.728 --> 01:01:30.979
Lila!

01:01:31.063 --> 01:01:32.605
(GRUNTING)

01:01:36.944 --> 01:01:39.279
Hey. Hey, look at me.

01:01:39.447 --> 01:01:40.572
You okay?

01:01:41.282 --> 01:01:43.324
Yeah. Yeah. (PANTING)

01:01:45.244 --> 01:01:46.411
It worked.

01:01:48.164 --> 01:01:49.539
It worked.

01:01:52.668 --> 01:01:54.502
STEVE: Okay, so the how works.

01:01:55.171 --> 01:01:58.214
Now, we gotta figure out
the when and the where.

01:01:59.049 --> 01:02:00.842
Almost everyone in this room
has had an encounter...

01:02:01.010 --> 01:02:02.677
with at least one of
the six Infinity Stones.

01:02:02.845 --> 01:02:04.345
Or substitute
the word "encounter"...

01:02:04.513 --> 01:02:05.597
for "damn near been killed"

01:02:05.681 --> 01:02:07.098
by one of
the six Infinity Stones.

01:02:07.266 --> 01:02:08.433
Well, I haven't...

01:02:08.517 --> 01:02:09.517
but I don't even know

01:02:09.602 --> 01:02:10.935
what the hell
you're all talking about.

01:02:11.103 --> 01:02:13.980
Regardless, we only have
enough Pym Particles

01:02:14.064 --> 01:02:15.857
for one round-trip each.

01:02:16.025 --> 01:02:17.233
And these stones have been

01:02:17.318 --> 01:02:19.235
in a lot of different places
throughout history.

01:02:19.403 --> 01:02:20.695
Our history.

01:02:20.863 --> 01:02:23.865
So, not a lot of convenient
spots to just drop in, yeah?

01:02:24.033 --> 01:02:25.825
Which means we have to
pick our targets.

01:02:26.285 --> 01:02:27.535
Correct.

01:02:28.913 --> 01:02:30.497
So, let's start
with the Aether.

01:02:30.664 --> 01:02:31.873
Thor, what do you know?

01:02:37.463 --> 01:02:38.671
NATASHA: Is he asleep?

01:02:38.839 --> 01:02:41.382
RHODES: No, no.
I'm pretty sure he's dead.

01:02:44.470 --> 01:02:46.137
Uh, where to start? Um...

01:02:47.806 --> 01:02:50.350
The Aether, firstly,
is not a stone.

01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:52.644
Someone called it
a stone before.

01:02:53.812 --> 01:02:58.024
Um, it's more of an angry
sludge sort of a thing...

01:02:58.192 --> 01:02:59.817
so someone's gonna need
to amend that

01:02:59.902 --> 01:03:01.069
and stop saying that.

01:03:01.529 --> 01:03:04.072
Here's an interesting story,
though, about the Aether.

01:03:04.240 --> 01:03:06.115
My grandfather,
many years ago...

01:03:06.283 --> 01:03:09.786
had to hide the stone
from the Dark Elves.

01:03:10.412 --> 01:03:12.664
Ooh. (CHUCKLES) Scary beings.

01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.541
So, Jane, actually...

01:03:15.125 --> 01:03:16.668
Oh, there she is.

01:03:17.127 --> 01:03:20.505
Yeah, so Jane was
an old flame of mine.

01:03:21.674 --> 01:03:24.717
You know, she stuck her hand
inside a rock this one time...

01:03:24.885 --> 01:03:27.720
and then the Aether
stuck itself inside her...

01:03:28.138 --> 01:03:29.931
and she became
very, very sick.

01:03:30.099 --> 01:03:31.975
And so I had to
take her to Asgard,

01:03:32.059 --> 01:03:33.226
which is where I'm from...

01:03:33.394 --> 01:03:35.353
and we had to try and fix her.

01:03:35.521 --> 01:03:37.146
We were dating at the time,
you see...

01:03:37.314 --> 01:03:40.692
and I got to introduce her
to my mother...

01:03:42.027 --> 01:03:44.070
(SIGHS) who's dead and, um...

01:03:45.489 --> 01:03:46.990
Oh, you know, Jane and I

01:03:47.074 --> 01:03:48.992
aren't even
dating anymore, so...

01:03:49.076 --> 01:03:50.076
(MOUTHING)

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:51.327
Yes, these things happen,
though. You know?

01:03:51.453 --> 01:03:52.787
Nothing lasts forever.
The only thing that...

01:03:52.871 --> 01:03:54.706
- Why don't you come sit down?
- I'm not done yet.

01:03:54.873 --> 01:03:56.416
The only thing
that is permanent in life

01:03:56.500 --> 01:03:57.917
is impermanence. (LAUGHS)

01:03:58.669 --> 01:04:00.962
Awesome.
Eggs? Breakfast?

01:04:01.130 --> 01:04:03.172
No. I'd like a Bloody Mary.

01:04:03.340 --> 01:04:05.466
ROCKET: Quill said he stole
the Power Stone from Morag.

01:04:06.552 --> 01:04:09.262
- SMART HULK: Is that a person?
- No, Morag's a planet.

01:04:09.972 --> 01:04:11.347
Quill was a person.

01:04:12.099 --> 01:04:14.434
Like a planet?
Like in outer space?

01:04:14.602 --> 01:04:16.019
Oh, look.

01:04:16.103 --> 01:04:18.813
It's like a little puppy,
all happy and everything.

01:04:18.981 --> 01:04:22.150
Do you wanna go to space?
You wanna go to space, puppy?

01:04:22.318 --> 01:04:23.443
I'll take you to space.

01:04:24.820 --> 01:04:26.738
NEBULA: Thanos found
the Soul Stone on Vormir.

01:04:26.905 --> 01:04:28.865
What is Vormir?

01:04:29.033 --> 01:04:30.199
NEBULA: A dominion of death...

01:04:30.909 --> 01:04:32.785
at the very center
of celestial existence.

01:04:34.705 --> 01:04:38.708
It's where
Thanos murdered my sister.

01:04:42.838 --> 01:04:43.963
(STEVE SIGHS)

01:04:45.132 --> 01:04:46.174
Not it.

01:04:48.010 --> 01:04:49.552
NATASHA: That Time Stone guy.
SMART HULK: Doctor Strange.

01:04:49.720 --> 01:04:51.512
NATASHA: Yeah,
what kind of doctor was he?

01:04:51.680 --> 01:04:53.640
TONY: Ear-nose-throat
meets rabbit-from-hat.

01:04:53.807 --> 01:04:55.183
SMART HULK: Nice place
in the Village, though.

01:04:55.267 --> 01:04:56.851
TONY: Yeah,
on Sullivan Street?

01:04:57.019 --> 01:04:58.061
SMART HULK:
Mm... Bleecker Street.

01:04:58.187 --> 01:04:59.270
Wait, he lived in New York?

01:04:59.855 --> 01:05:00.897
TONY: No, he lived in Toronto.

01:05:00.981 --> 01:05:02.023
Uh, yeah,
on Bleecker and Sullivan.

01:05:02.107 --> 01:05:03.107
Have you been listening
to anything?

01:05:03.192 --> 01:05:04.192
Guys.

01:05:04.276 --> 01:05:05.943
If you pick the right year,

01:05:06.028 --> 01:05:07.654
there are three stones
in New York.

01:05:10.115 --> 01:05:11.824
Shut the front door.

01:05:14.578 --> 01:05:16.704
STEVE: All right.
We have a plan.

01:05:16.872 --> 01:05:21.459
Six stones, three teams,
one shot.

01:05:31.178 --> 01:05:33.054
<i>STEVE: Five years ago,</i>
<i>we lost.</i>

01:05:34.390 --> 01:05:35.682
<i>All of us.</i>

01:05:37.601 --> 01:05:38.976
<i>We lost friends.</i>

01:05:39.687 --> 01:05:41.354
<i>We lost family.</i>

01:05:43.315 --> 01:05:45.149
<i>We lost a part of ourselves.</i>

01:05:46.610 --> 01:05:48.945
<i>Today, we have a chance</i>
<i>to take it all back.</i>

01:05:50.364 --> 01:05:53.199
<i>You know your teams.</i>
<i>You know your missions.</i>

01:05:54.034 --> 01:05:55.952
<i>Get the stones. Get them back.</i>

01:05:56.787 --> 01:05:57.954
One round-trip each.

01:05:58.122 --> 01:05:59.205
No mistakes...

01:05:59.707 --> 01:06:01.416
no do-overs.

01:06:01.583 --> 01:06:03.459
Most of us are going
somewhere we know.

01:06:03.627 --> 01:06:05.461
That doesn't mean
we should know what to expect.

01:06:06.630 --> 01:06:07.630
Be careful.

01:06:08.298 --> 01:06:09.549
Look out for each other.

01:06:11.009 --> 01:06:12.802
This is the fight
of our lives...

01:06:13.679 --> 01:06:15.263
and we're gonna win.

01:06:17.433 --> 01:06:18.433
Whatever it takes.

01:06:21.687 --> 01:06:23.146
Good luck.

01:06:23.313 --> 01:06:24.397
He's pretty good at that.

01:06:24.565 --> 01:06:25.732
- Right?
- TONY: All right.

01:06:25.899 --> 01:06:26.899
You heard the man.

01:06:26.984 --> 01:06:28.234
Stroke those keys,
Jolly Green.

01:06:29.194 --> 01:06:30.737
SMART HULK: Trackers engaged.

01:06:31.530 --> 01:06:33.364
You promise to bring that back
in one piece, right?

01:06:33.532 --> 01:06:34.866
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:06:35.033 --> 01:06:36.909
Okay, I'll do my best.

01:06:37.077 --> 01:06:38.870
As promises go,
that was pretty lame.

01:06:41.498 --> 01:06:43.082
- (BEEPING)
- See ya in a minute.

01:07:16.366 --> 01:07:17.742
(CHITAURI SNARLING)

01:07:19.453 --> 01:07:20.495
(ROARS)

01:07:20.579 --> 01:07:22.830
(ROARING)

01:07:37.513 --> 01:07:38.805
All right, we all have
our assignments.

01:07:38.972 --> 01:07:41.182
Two stones uptown,
one stone down.

01:07:41.350 --> 01:07:43.267
Stay low.
Keep an eye on the clock.

01:07:43.352 --> 01:07:44.435
(THUD)

01:07:50.943 --> 01:07:52.318
(ROARING)

01:07:58.742 --> 01:08:00.535
Maybe smash
a few things along the way.

01:08:01.662 --> 01:08:03.663
I think it's gratuitous,
but whatever.

01:08:06.250 --> 01:08:07.959
(ROARING SOFTLY)

01:08:15.968 --> 01:08:16.968
(ROARS SOFTLY)

01:08:31.400 --> 01:08:32.859
ANCIENT ONE:
I'd be careful going that way.

01:08:32.943 --> 01:08:34.569
We just had the floors waxed.

01:08:39.908 --> 01:08:41.534
Yeah, I'm looking
for Doctor Strange.

01:08:43.120 --> 01:08:45.997
You're about
five years too early.

01:08:46.790 --> 01:08:48.916
Stephen Strange is currently
performing surgery

01:08:49.001 --> 01:08:50.501
about 20 blocks that way.

01:08:52.296 --> 01:08:53.296
What do you want from him?

01:08:54.214 --> 01:08:55.214
That, actually.

01:08:56.174 --> 01:08:57.258
Ah!

01:08:58.427 --> 01:08:59.427
I'm afraid not.

01:08:59.845 --> 01:09:01.220
Sorry, but I wasn't asking.

01:09:02.139 --> 01:09:03.139
You don't want to do this.

01:09:03.307 --> 01:09:04.974
Ah, you're right, I don't.
But I need that stone...

01:09:05.058 --> 01:09:06.559
and I don't have time
to debate it.

01:09:07.394 --> 01:09:08.644
(GRUNTS)

01:09:15.569 --> 01:09:17.153
Let's start over, shall we?

01:09:28.707 --> 01:09:30.291
ASGARDIAN MAIDEN:
For you, Lady Jane.

01:09:30.375 --> 01:09:32.752
JANE: Um, so you have anything
with pants?

01:09:32.920 --> 01:09:34.045
ASGARDIAN MAIDEN: Pants?

01:09:34.129 --> 01:09:36.213
JANE: Never mind.
These will be fine. Thank you.

01:09:36.381 --> 01:09:38.007
ASGARDIAN MAIDEN: Yes, milady.
THOR: Oh, there's Jane.

01:09:39.635 --> 01:09:40.635
All right.

01:09:42.220 --> 01:09:43.471
Here's the deal, tubby.

01:09:43.639 --> 01:09:44.680
You're gonna charm her,

01:09:44.765 --> 01:09:46.015
and I'm gonna poke her
with this thing...

01:09:46.183 --> 01:09:48.643
and extract the Reality Stone,
and get gone lickety-split.

01:09:48.852 --> 01:09:50.019
(SNIFFS)

01:09:50.395 --> 01:09:51.520
I'll be right back, okay?

01:09:51.605 --> 01:09:53.356
The wine cellar
is just down here.

01:09:53.523 --> 01:09:56.400
My father used to have this
huge barrel of Aakonian ale.

01:09:56.568 --> 01:09:57.944
I'll see if the scullery has
a couple of to-go cups.

01:09:58.028 --> 01:09:59.862
Hey. Hey! Aren't you
drunk enough already?

01:09:59.947 --> 01:10:02.031
(DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)

01:10:07.245 --> 01:10:08.245
If you could send Loki
some soup.

01:10:08.330 --> 01:10:09.330
Yes, milady.

01:10:09.414 --> 01:10:10.414
And ask our librarians

01:10:10.499 --> 01:10:13.334
to pull some volumes
from the astronomy shelf.

01:10:19.508 --> 01:10:21.050
Who's the fancy broad?

01:10:22.386 --> 01:10:23.886
That's my mother.

01:10:24.388 --> 01:10:26.097
She dies today.

01:10:26.765 --> 01:10:28.557
Oh, that is today?

01:10:31.812 --> 01:10:34.021
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

01:10:35.107 --> 01:10:37.650
I can't do this.
I can't do this.

01:10:38.235 --> 01:10:39.777
I shouldn't be here.
I shouldn't have come.

01:10:39.945 --> 01:10:41.070
It's a bad idea!

01:10:41.363 --> 01:10:42.405
- Come here.
- No, no, no.

01:10:42.572 --> 01:10:44.991
I think I'm having
a panic attack.

01:10:45.075 --> 01:10:46.075
Come here. Right here.

01:10:46.159 --> 01:10:47.159
I shouldn't be here.
This is bad.

01:10:47.953 --> 01:10:49.662
You think you're the only one
who lost people?

01:10:49.746 --> 01:10:51.580
What do you think
we're doing here?

01:10:51.748 --> 01:10:53.916
I lost the only family
I ever had.

01:10:54.084 --> 01:10:56.502
Quill, Groot, Drax,
the chick with the antenna...

01:10:56.670 --> 01:10:58.087
all gone.

01:10:58.797 --> 01:11:00.131
I get you miss your mom...

01:11:00.424 --> 01:11:01.632
but she's gone.

01:11:01.800 --> 01:11:02.800
Really gone.

01:11:03.385 --> 01:11:06.220
And there are plenty of people
who are only kind of gone...

01:11:06.388 --> 01:11:07.513
and you can help them.

01:11:08.640 --> 01:11:10.141
So, is it too much to ask

01:11:10.225 --> 01:11:11.851
that you brush the crumbs
out of your beard...

01:11:12.019 --> 01:11:14.311
make schmoopy talk
to Pretty Pants...

01:11:14.771 --> 01:11:17.648
and when she's not looking,
suck out the Infinity Stone...

01:11:17.816 --> 01:11:19.400
and help me
get my family back?

01:11:20.610 --> 01:11:22.069
(SIGHS) Okay.

01:11:22.362 --> 01:11:23.362
Are you crying?

01:11:23.989 --> 01:11:25.281
(SOBBING) No.

01:11:27.117 --> 01:11:28.284
Yes.

01:11:28.452 --> 01:11:29.660
I feel like I'm losing it.

01:11:29.828 --> 01:11:30.828
Get it together!

01:11:30.996 --> 01:11:32.830
- You can do this.
- (EXHALES)

01:11:33.081 --> 01:11:34.498
You can do this.

01:11:36.084 --> 01:11:37.585
(TAKING DEEP BREATHS)

01:11:37.669 --> 01:11:38.669
All right?

01:11:38.837 --> 01:11:39.837
Yes, I can.

01:11:40.005 --> 01:11:41.005
Good.

01:11:43.216 --> 01:11:45.551
I can do this. I can do this.

01:11:46.386 --> 01:11:47.845
I can't do this.

01:11:48.013 --> 01:11:49.889
All right, heartbreaker,
she's alone.

01:11:49.973 --> 01:11:51.432
This is our shot.

01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:54.185
Thor? Thor!

01:11:55.145 --> 01:11:56.145
(GROANS)

01:12:04.488 --> 01:12:05.821
WAR MACHINE: All right,
bring it down, Blue.

01:12:05.989 --> 01:12:08.407
Right on that line. That's it.
Down, down.

01:12:11.369 --> 01:12:12.453
(SNARLS)

01:12:13.205 --> 01:12:14.747
- (SIGHS)
- Hey, can we hurry it up?

01:12:14.915 --> 01:12:16.999
Guys, chop-chop. Come on.
We're on the clock.

01:12:17.167 --> 01:12:18.918
All that is really helpful.

01:12:21.129 --> 01:12:22.630
- Take care, okay?
- Yeah.

01:12:22.798 --> 01:12:25.257
Get that stone and come back.
No messing around.

01:12:25.801 --> 01:12:27.468
- Hey.
- We got this.

01:12:27.636 --> 01:12:28.844
- Let's get it done.
- Yes, sir.

01:12:29.012 --> 01:12:30.304
I'll see you back.

01:12:31.014 --> 01:12:32.348
You guys watch
each other's six.

01:12:33.016 --> 01:12:34.266
Yeah.

01:12:42.943 --> 01:12:44.485
NEBULA: Coordinates for Vormir
are laid in.

01:12:46.113 --> 01:12:48.030
All they have to do
is not fall out.

01:12:53.954 --> 01:12:56.330
We're a long way
from Budapest.

01:12:56.414 --> 01:12:57.623
(CHUCKLES)

01:13:01.211 --> 01:13:02.711
Okay, so, uh...

01:13:03.964 --> 01:13:07.174
we just wait around for
this Quill guy to show up...

01:13:07.342 --> 01:13:09.176
and then he leads us to
the Power Stone, is that it?

01:13:10.178 --> 01:13:11.595
Let's take cover.

01:13:13.223 --> 01:13:15.683
We're not the only ones in
2014 looking for the stones.

01:13:15.767 --> 01:13:17.184
Wait a minute. What are you
talking about right now?

01:13:17.269 --> 01:13:18.602
Who else is looking
for these stones?

01:13:22.232 --> 01:13:23.649
My father...

01:13:23.817 --> 01:13:25.609
my sister...

01:13:25.777 --> 01:13:26.902
and me.

01:13:27.070 --> 01:13:28.237
And you?

01:13:30.115 --> 01:13:31.699
Where are you right now?

01:13:32.617 --> 01:13:33.617
(YELLING)

01:13:40.917 --> 01:13:42.376
(BEEPING)

01:13:43.545 --> 01:13:45.171
(GRUNTING)

01:13:47.549 --> 01:13:48.549
(YELLING)

01:13:54.139 --> 01:13:55.389
(SIGHS)

01:13:56.474 --> 01:13:57.683
(GRUNTS)

01:14:00.395 --> 01:14:01.562
GAMORA: You're welcome.

01:14:01.730 --> 01:14:04.023
I didn't ask for your help.

01:14:04.691 --> 01:14:06.317
And yet, you always need it.

01:14:07.110 --> 01:14:08.736
- (SIGHS)
- (GAMORA CHUCKLES)

01:14:10.363 --> 01:14:12.364
Get up. Father wants us
back on the ship.

01:14:12.532 --> 01:14:13.532
Why?

01:14:13.700 --> 01:14:15.701
He's found an Infinity Stone.

01:14:20.207 --> 01:14:21.665
2014 NEBULA: Where?

01:14:21.833 --> 01:14:23.584
GAMORA: On a planet
called Morag.

01:14:25.212 --> 01:14:27.129
Father's plan
is finally in motion.

01:14:27.297 --> 01:14:29.298
One stone isn't six, Nebula.

01:14:29.466 --> 01:14:30.674
It's a start.

01:14:30.842 --> 01:14:32.635
If he gets all of them...

01:14:35.013 --> 01:14:36.430
(THUD)

01:14:45.649 --> 01:14:47.399
Ronan's located
the Power Stone.

01:14:47.484 --> 01:14:49.193
I'm dispatching you
to his ship.

01:14:49.361 --> 01:14:50.569
He won't like that.

01:14:50.737 --> 01:14:52.863
His alternative is death.

01:14:54.366 --> 01:14:56.116
Ronan's obsession...

01:14:57.160 --> 01:14:59.328
clouds his judgment.

01:15:03.750 --> 01:15:05.542
We will not fail you, Father.

01:15:06.586 --> 01:15:08.212
No, you won't.

01:15:10.924 --> 01:15:11.924
I swear...

01:15:13.802 --> 01:15:15.719
I will make you proud.

01:15:17.138 --> 01:15:19.181
(GROANING)

01:15:24.104 --> 01:15:27.773
<i>...we just wait around for</i>
<i>this Quill guy to show up...</i>

01:15:27.941 --> 01:15:29.942
<i>and then he leads us to</i>
<i>the Power Stone, is that it?</i>

01:15:30.110 --> 01:15:31.694
NEBULA: Let's take cover.

01:15:32.696 --> 01:15:35.572
<i>We're not the only ones in</i>
<i>2014 looking for the stones.</i>

01:15:36.199 --> 01:15:37.324
(GRUNTS)

01:15:37.993 --> 01:15:39.451
Who was that?

01:15:39.619 --> 01:15:40.703
I don't know. (GASPING)

01:15:40.787 --> 01:15:42.955
My head is splitting.
I don't know.

01:15:44.416 --> 01:15:47.376
Her synaptic drive was
probably damaged in battle.

01:15:48.044 --> 01:15:49.378
Shh.

01:15:57.637 --> 01:15:59.680
Bring her to my ship.

01:16:07.147 --> 01:16:08.147
IRON MAN: Better hustle, Cap.

01:16:08.315 --> 01:16:10.399
Things look like they're
just about wrapped up here.

01:16:10.483 --> 01:16:12.192
CAPTAIN AMERICA: Got it. I'm
<i>approaching the elevator now.</i>

01:16:18.658 --> 01:16:20.242
LOKI: If it's all the same
to you...

01:16:22.537 --> 01:16:24.079
I'll have that drink now.

01:16:24.622 --> 01:16:26.081
2012 IRON MAN: All right,
get him on his feet.

01:16:26.249 --> 01:16:29.251
We can all stand around
posing up a storm later.

01:16:29.419 --> 01:16:30.753
By the way,
feel free to clean up.

01:16:31.087 --> 01:16:33.922
(SCOFFS) Mr. Rogers, I almost
forgot that that suit...

01:16:34.090 --> 01:16:35.799
did nothing for your ass.

01:16:35.884 --> 01:16:37.259
CAPTAIN AMERICA: No one
<i>asked you to look, Tony.</i>

01:16:37.344 --> 01:16:38.344
It's ridiculous.

01:16:38.428 --> 01:16:39.553
ANT-MAN:
<i>I think you look great, Cap.</i>

01:16:39.637 --> 01:16:42.056
<i>As far as I'm concerned,</i>
<i>that's America's ass.</i>

01:16:42.265 --> 01:16:44.099
2012 BLACK WIDOW:
Who gets the, uh, magic wand?

01:16:44.184 --> 01:16:45.392
2012 CAPTAIN AMERICA:
S.T.R.I.K.E. team's

01:16:45.477 --> 01:16:46.643
- coming to secure it.
- (ELEVATOR BEEPS)

01:16:56.571 --> 01:16:58.322
SITWELL: We can take that
off your hands.

01:16:58.490 --> 01:16:59.490
By all means.

01:17:01.743 --> 01:17:03.452
Careful with that thing.

01:17:03.620 --> 01:17:05.079
Yeah, unless you want
your mind erased.

01:17:05.246 --> 01:17:06.246
And not in a fun way.

01:17:06.373 --> 01:17:07.373
We promise to be careful.

01:17:07.457 --> 01:17:08.582
ANT-MAN: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>Who are these guys?</i>

01:17:08.750 --> 01:17:10.042
They are S.H.I.E.L.D.

01:17:10.210 --> 01:17:13.295
Well, actually Hydra,
but we didn't know that yet.

01:17:13.463 --> 01:17:15.631
ANT-MAN: Seriously?
<i>You didn't?</i>

01:17:15.799 --> 01:17:17.299
<i>I mean,</i>
<i>they look like bad guys.</i>

01:17:17.467 --> 01:17:18.884
You're small,
but you're talking loud.

01:17:19.052 --> 01:17:20.886
On my way down to coordinate
search and rescue.

01:17:21.054 --> 01:17:23.013
On my way down to coordinate
search and rescue.

01:17:23.181 --> 01:17:25.641
I mean, honestly, how do you
keep your food down?

01:17:25.809 --> 01:17:27.226
Shut up.

01:17:27.811 --> 01:17:29.103
Ooh. All right, you're up,
little buddy.

01:17:29.270 --> 01:17:31.397
There's our stone.

01:17:31.564 --> 01:17:32.564
<i>ANT-MAN: All right.</i>

01:17:32.732 --> 01:17:33.899
<i>Flick me.</i>

01:17:47.997 --> 01:17:49.081
- Move.
- Hey.

01:17:49.165 --> 01:17:50.916
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Hey, hey. Buddy!

01:17:51.084 --> 01:17:52.876
What do you think? Maximum
occupancy has been reached.

01:17:52.961 --> 01:17:54.044
- (GROWLS)
- Take the stairs.

01:17:54.212 --> 01:17:55.796
2012 TONY: Yeah. Stop, stop.

01:17:55.880 --> 01:17:57.256
(ROARS)

01:17:58.842 --> 01:18:02.219
"Take the stairs."
Hate the stairs. (GRUNTS)

01:18:05.348 --> 01:18:07.724
All right, Cap, I got
our scepter in the elevator...

01:18:07.892 --> 01:18:09.685
just passing the 80th floor.

01:18:10.478 --> 01:18:11.478
On it.

01:18:12.063 --> 01:18:13.063
Head to the lobby.

01:18:13.148 --> 01:18:14.189
IRON MAN: All right,
<i>I'll see you there.</i>

01:18:14.566 --> 01:18:16.150
SITWELL: Evidence secure.

01:18:16.317 --> 01:18:17.734
We're en route to Doctor List.

01:18:18.445 --> 01:18:21.321
No. No hitches at all,
Mr. Secretary.

01:18:26.494 --> 01:18:27.494
Captain.

01:18:27.579 --> 01:18:28.704
I thought
you were coordinating

01:18:28.788 --> 01:18:29.788
search and rescue.

01:18:29.873 --> 01:18:31.415
CAPTAIN AMERICA:
Change of plans.

01:18:35.253 --> 01:18:36.670
Hey, Cap.

01:18:37.964 --> 01:18:39.006
Rumlow.

01:18:45.305 --> 01:18:47.139
I just got a call
from the secretary.

01:18:47.307 --> 01:18:49.183
I'm gonna be running point
on the scepter.

01:18:51.686 --> 01:18:53.937
Sir?
I don't understand.

01:18:56.399 --> 01:18:58.233
We got word there may be
an attempt to steal it.

01:18:58.401 --> 01:18:59.985
Sorry, Cap.

01:19:00.153 --> 01:19:01.570
We can't give you the scepter.

01:19:02.155 --> 01:19:04.031
I'm gonna have to call
the director.

01:19:04.199 --> 01:19:06.325
That's okay. Trust me.

01:19:09.829 --> 01:19:10.829
Hail Hydra.

01:19:15.001 --> 01:19:16.168
(ELEVATOR BEEPS)

01:19:24.219 --> 01:19:25.469
(GROANS)

01:19:25.553 --> 01:19:27.429
So many stairs!

01:19:27.514 --> 01:19:28.722
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

01:19:30.892 --> 01:19:32.226
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

01:19:39.150 --> 01:19:41.777
Thumbelina, do you copy?
I've got eyes on the prize.

01:19:41.945 --> 01:19:43.028
It is go time.

01:19:43.112 --> 01:19:44.196
ANT-MAN: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>Bombs away.</i>

01:19:45.240 --> 01:19:46.240
(ANT-MAN GRUNTS)

01:19:51.454 --> 01:19:53.830
<i>Is that Axe Body Spray?</i>

01:19:53.998 --> 01:19:56.291
Yeah, I had a can in the desk
for emergencies. Relax.

01:19:56.376 --> 01:19:57.459
Can we focus, please?

01:19:57.627 --> 01:19:58.877
ANT-MAN:
<i>I'm going inside you...</i>

01:19:59.587 --> 01:20:00.587
now.

01:20:06.469 --> 01:20:08.011
Uh, may I ask you
where you're going?

01:20:08.096 --> 01:20:10.430
Bit of lunch and then Asgard.
I'm sorry, you are...?

01:20:10.515 --> 01:20:11.598
Alexander Pierce.

01:20:11.683 --> 01:20:12.975
He's the man above the folks

01:20:13.059 --> 01:20:14.226
- behind Nick Fury.
- Oh.

01:20:14.310 --> 01:20:15.519
My friends call me
Mr. Secretary.

01:20:15.603 --> 01:20:16.603
I'm gonna have to ask you

01:20:16.688 --> 01:20:17.980
to turn that prisoner
over to me.

01:20:18.064 --> 01:20:19.940
Uh, Loki will be answering
to Odin himself.

01:20:20.024 --> 01:20:21.108
PIERCE: No, he's going
to answer to us.

01:20:21.192 --> 01:20:22.484
Odin can have what's left.

01:20:22.652 --> 01:20:24.111
And I'm gonna need that case.

01:20:24.279 --> 01:20:26.071
That's been S.H.I.E.L.D.
property for over 70 years.

01:20:26.239 --> 01:20:27.239
Hand over the case, Stark.

01:20:27.323 --> 01:20:28.782
(INHALES SHARPLY) All right,
move it, Stuart Little.

01:20:28.866 --> 01:20:30.075
Things are getting dicey
out here. Let's go.

01:20:30.159 --> 01:20:31.868
I'm not gonna argue who's got
the higher authority here...

01:20:32.328 --> 01:20:33.620
ANT-MAN: You promise me
<i>you won't die?</i>

01:20:33.788 --> 01:20:36.498
We're only giving me
a mild cardiac dysrhythmia.

01:20:36.666 --> 01:20:38.250
ANT-MAN:
<i>That doesn't sound mild.</i>

01:20:38.418 --> 01:20:39.418
I need the case.

01:20:39.502 --> 01:20:40.877
I know you got a lot of pull,
I'm just saying,

01:20:40.962 --> 01:20:42.296
- jurisdiction...
- Okay, then give me the case.

01:20:42.463 --> 01:20:43.463
2012 TONY:
Well, jurisdiction...

01:20:43.548 --> 01:20:44.548
AGENT: Hand it over.

01:20:44.632 --> 01:20:45.632
Do it, Lang!

01:20:45.717 --> 01:20:46.717
Get your hands off me.

01:20:46.801 --> 01:20:48.260
Window's closing. Pull my pin.

01:20:48.720 --> 01:20:49.970
ANT-MAN: Here goes!

01:20:50.054 --> 01:20:51.638
(GASPING AND CHOKING)

01:20:52.807 --> 01:20:54.349
- Stark?
- 2012 THOR: Stark?

01:20:55.685 --> 01:20:56.852
AGENT: He's convulsing.
Give him air!

01:20:56.936 --> 01:20:58.645
- Medic!
- Medic!

01:20:59.188 --> 01:21:00.564
Give these guys some help.

01:21:00.940 --> 01:21:02.316
- 2012 THOR: Speak to me.
- (GASPING)

01:21:02.400 --> 01:21:04.192
(STAMMERS) Stark,
is it your chest machine?

01:21:06.946 --> 01:21:08.280
Breathe, breathe.

01:21:13.536 --> 01:21:14.786
TONY: Good job.
Meet me in the alley.

01:21:14.871 --> 01:21:15.871
I'm gonna grab a quick slice.

01:21:16.956 --> 01:21:18.040
(HULK ROARS)

01:21:21.586 --> 01:21:23.295
No stairs!

01:21:23.671 --> 01:21:25.255
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

01:21:30.428 --> 01:21:32.804
Uh... Come on, Stark,
stay with us.

01:21:32.889 --> 01:21:33.889
I'm going to try something.
Okay?

01:21:33.973 --> 01:21:35.098
I have no idea
if it's going to work.

01:21:35.767 --> 01:21:37.934
- (GRUNTS, EXHALES)
- Yes!

01:21:38.102 --> 01:21:39.478
Oh, that worked a treat.

01:21:39.646 --> 01:21:40.646
Dude, that was so crazy.

01:21:40.813 --> 01:21:42.189
I had no idea
if that was gonna work.

01:21:42.357 --> 01:21:44.232
- The case.
- The case is, uh...

01:21:44.400 --> 01:21:46.401
Where's the case?
Where's Loki?

01:21:47.403 --> 01:21:48.403
Loki!

01:21:48.488 --> 01:21:49.946
ANT-MAN: That wasn't supposed
<i>to happen, was it?</i>

01:21:50.031 --> 01:21:51.114
Oh, we blew it.

01:21:51.199 --> 01:21:52.699
Loki?

01:21:52.784 --> 01:21:54.242
(ALARM BLARING)

01:21:54.744 --> 01:21:56.036
Tony, what's going on?

01:21:57.038 --> 01:21:58.705
Tell me you found that Cube.

01:22:00.333 --> 01:22:01.500
(SIGHS)

01:22:01.584 --> 01:22:03.001
Oh, you gotta be shitting me.

01:22:07.090 --> 01:22:09.299
I have eyes on Loki.
14th floor.

01:22:09.467 --> 01:22:10.842
I'm not Loki...

01:22:14.430 --> 01:22:16.056
and I don't wanna hurt you.

01:22:19.310 --> 01:22:20.686
(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:22:23.773 --> 01:22:24.898
(PANTS)

01:22:24.982 --> 01:22:25.982
I can do this all day.

01:22:26.150 --> 01:22:27.442
Yeah, I know.

01:22:27.610 --> 01:22:28.610
I know.

01:22:29.570 --> 01:22:30.779
(BOTH GRUNT)

01:22:52.510 --> 01:22:53.510
(PANTS)

01:22:59.308 --> 01:23:00.434
(PANTING)

01:23:01.352 --> 01:23:02.352
Where did you get this?

01:23:05.398 --> 01:23:07.149
(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:23:13.656 --> 01:23:16.700
Bucky is alive.

01:23:19.162 --> 01:23:20.162
(COUGHS)

01:23:20.246 --> 01:23:21.288
What?

01:23:31.007 --> 01:23:32.424
(PANTING)

01:23:36.220 --> 01:23:37.763
That is America's ass.

01:23:42.143 --> 01:23:43.226
BANNER: Please, please.

01:23:43.311 --> 01:23:45.187
I'm sorry,
I can't help you, Bruce.

01:23:46.230 --> 01:23:47.564
If I give up the Time Stone

01:23:47.648 --> 01:23:49.357
to help your reality,
I'm dooming my own.

01:23:49.525 --> 01:23:51.276
With all due respect,
all right...

01:23:51.444 --> 01:23:54.529
I'm not sure the science
really supports that.

01:24:00.161 --> 01:24:02.120
The Infinity Stones create

01:24:02.205 --> 01:24:04.456
what you experience
as the flow of time.

01:24:04.624 --> 01:24:06.166
Remove one of the stones...

01:24:06.334 --> 01:24:08.418
and that flow splits.

01:24:08.586 --> 01:24:11.046
Now, this may benefit
your reality...

01:24:11.214 --> 01:24:13.340
but my new one, not so much.

01:24:13.716 --> 01:24:15.425
In this new branch reality...

01:24:15.593 --> 01:24:17.260
without our chief weapon

01:24:17.345 --> 01:24:18.678
against the forces
of darkness...

01:24:19.096 --> 01:24:21.014
our world would be overrun.

01:24:21.182 --> 01:24:22.891
Millions will suffer.

01:24:23.059 --> 01:24:24.309
So, tell me, Doctor.

01:24:24.894 --> 01:24:27.062
Can your science
prevent all that?

01:24:27.230 --> 01:24:28.230
No...

01:24:29.232 --> 01:24:30.357
but we can erase it.

01:24:30.525 --> 01:24:32.234
Because once we're done
with the stones...

01:24:32.401 --> 01:24:34.569
we can return each one
to its own timeline...

01:24:34.737 --> 01:24:36.238
at the moment it was taken.

01:24:36.405 --> 01:24:38.865
So, chronologically...

01:24:39.909 --> 01:24:40.951
in that reality...

01:24:43.538 --> 01:24:45.205
it never left.

01:24:47.583 --> 01:24:50.669
Yes, but you're leaving out
the most important part.

01:24:54.257 --> 01:24:56.716
In order to return the stones,
you have to survive.

01:24:56.884 --> 01:24:59.469
We will. I will. I promise.

01:25:00.304 --> 01:25:02.347
I can't risk this reality
on a promise.

01:25:04.016 --> 01:25:06.768
It's the duty
of the Sorcerer Supreme

01:25:06.853 --> 01:25:08.645
to protect the Time Stone.

01:25:09.021 --> 01:25:10.897
Then why the hell did
Strange give it away?

01:25:12.859 --> 01:25:13.942
What did you say?

01:25:14.110 --> 01:25:16.444
Strange. He gave it away.
He gave it to Thanos.

01:25:17.071 --> 01:25:18.655
- Willingly?
- Yes.

01:25:22.577 --> 01:25:24.244
- Why?
- I have no idea.

01:25:24.328 --> 01:25:26.079
Maybe he made a mistake.

01:25:36.215 --> 01:25:37.507
Or I did.

01:25:57.778 --> 01:26:00.196
Strange is meant to be
the best of us.

01:26:00.364 --> 01:26:02.866
So, he must've done it
for a reason.

01:26:03.659 --> 01:26:05.285
I fear you might be right.

01:26:08.247 --> 01:26:09.372
(SMART HULK SIGHS)

01:26:10.458 --> 01:26:11.458
Thank you.

01:26:17.715 --> 01:26:19.382
I'm counting on you, Bruce.

01:26:21.427 --> 01:26:22.636
We all are.

01:26:43.115 --> 01:26:44.658
Run diagnostics.

01:26:45.409 --> 01:26:47.369
Show me her memory file.

01:26:48.955 --> 01:26:51.414
Sire, the file
appears entangled.

01:26:52.583 --> 01:26:54.542
It was a memory, but not hers.

01:26:55.795 --> 01:26:57.212
There's another
consciousness...

01:26:57.380 --> 01:26:58.672
sharing her network.

01:26:59.215 --> 01:27:00.548
Another Nebula.

01:27:02.677 --> 01:27:04.135
Impossible.

01:27:04.303 --> 01:27:06.930
EBONY MAW: This duplicate
carries a time stamp...

01:27:07.848 --> 01:27:10.016
from nine years in the future.

01:27:14.605 --> 01:27:17.107
Where is this other Nebula?

01:27:17.775 --> 01:27:19.776
EBONY MAW: In our solar system
on Morag.

01:27:21.320 --> 01:27:22.612
Can you access her?

01:27:22.780 --> 01:27:24.823
EBONY MAW:
Yes, the two are linked.

01:27:24.991 --> 01:27:27.075
Search the duplicate's
memories...

01:27:27.243 --> 01:27:29.452
for Infinity Stones.

01:27:32.999 --> 01:27:34.165
BANNER:
<i>And these stones have been</i>

01:27:34.250 --> 01:27:35.959
<i>in a lot of different places</i>
<i>throughout history.</i>

01:27:36.127 --> 01:27:37.210
<i>Our history.</i>

01:27:37.294 --> 01:27:39.421
<i>So, not a lot</i>
<i>of convenient spots</i>

01:27:39.588 --> 01:27:40.714
<i>to just drop in.</i>

01:27:40.881 --> 01:27:42.549
BARTON: Which means
<i>we have to pick our targets.</i>

01:27:42.717 --> 01:27:44.009
TONY: Correct.
THANOS: Freeze image.

01:27:45.970 --> 01:27:47.178
GAMORA: Terrans.

01:27:48.264 --> 01:27:49.931
Avengers.

01:27:51.017 --> 01:27:52.726
Unruly wretches.

01:27:52.893 --> 01:27:54.394
What's that reflection?

01:27:56.022 --> 01:27:57.188
Amplify this, Maw.

01:28:00.693 --> 01:28:01.901
GAMORA: I don't understand.

01:28:06.615 --> 01:28:08.199
Two Nebulas.

01:28:08.367 --> 01:28:10.785
THANOS: No.
The same Nebula...

01:28:11.579 --> 01:28:13.329
from two different times.

01:28:14.623 --> 01:28:16.249
Set course for Morag.

01:28:16.417 --> 01:28:18.793
And scan
the duplicate's memories.

01:28:19.545 --> 01:28:21.921
I wanna see everything.

01:28:31.807 --> 01:28:33.767
My ladies, I'll see you after.

01:28:33.851 --> 01:28:35.268
I'll see you after.
Go on ahead.

01:28:49.658 --> 01:28:50.658
What are you doing?

01:28:50.743 --> 01:28:51.910
- (THOR SCREAMS)
- (SHRIEKS)

01:28:51.994 --> 01:28:53.495
- (GASPS)
- FRIGGA: Oh, God!

01:28:53.662 --> 01:28:56.122
You're better off leaving
the sneaking to your brother.

01:28:56.248 --> 01:28:58.124
No, I wasn't sneaking.
I was just going for a walk.

01:28:58.292 --> 01:28:59.626
What are you wearing?

01:28:59.794 --> 01:29:02.170
I always wear this.
It's one of my favorites.

01:29:02.254 --> 01:29:03.254
(CLEARS THROAT)

01:29:05.132 --> 01:29:06.174
THOR: Mm...

01:29:06.258 --> 01:29:07.634
What's wrong with your eye?

01:29:07.802 --> 01:29:08.802
Oh, my eye.

01:29:08.969 --> 01:29:10.929
Remember the, uh,
Battle of Harokin...

01:29:11.097 --> 01:29:12.347
when I got hit in the face

01:29:12.431 --> 01:29:14.182
with the broadsword?
(CHUCKLES)

01:29:17.686 --> 01:29:19.729
You're not the Thor
I know at all, are you?

01:29:20.481 --> 01:29:22.232
Yes, I am.

01:29:22.733 --> 01:29:25.235
The future hasn't been kind
to you, has it?

01:29:25.694 --> 01:29:27.612
I didn't say
I was from the future.

01:29:28.072 --> 01:29:30.615
I was raised by witches, boy.

01:29:31.659 --> 01:29:34.035
I see with more than eyes,
you know that.

01:29:36.122 --> 01:29:38.373
(VOICE BREAKING) Yeah,
I'm totally from the future.

01:29:38.541 --> 01:29:40.166
Yes, you are, honey.

01:29:40.334 --> 01:29:41.835
I really need to talk to you.

01:29:42.002 --> 01:29:43.002
We can talk.

01:29:48.217 --> 01:29:49.884
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

01:30:07.153 --> 01:30:09.112
His head was over there...

01:30:09.738 --> 01:30:12.240
and his body over there...

01:30:13.242 --> 01:30:16.035
(SCOFFS) I mean, what was
the point? I was too late.

01:30:16.704 --> 01:30:18.329
I was just standing there.

01:30:19.290 --> 01:30:21.040
Some idiot with an axe.

01:30:21.208 --> 01:30:22.917
FRIGGA: Now, you're no idiot.

01:30:24.044 --> 01:30:25.628
You're here, aren't you?

01:30:25.838 --> 01:30:28.298
Seeking counsel from
the wisest person in Asgard.

01:30:28.632 --> 01:30:29.674
I am. Yes.

01:30:29.842 --> 01:30:31.176
FRIGGA: Idiot, no.

01:30:31.343 --> 01:30:32.844
A failure?

01:30:33.012 --> 01:30:34.137
Absolutely.

01:30:34.305 --> 01:30:36.097
That's a little bit harsh.

01:30:36.265 --> 01:30:37.765
Do you know
what that makes you?

01:30:38.976 --> 01:30:40.977
Just like everyone else.

01:30:41.145 --> 01:30:43.229
I'm not supposed to be
like everyone else, am I?

01:30:43.314 --> 01:30:44.439
FRIGGA: Mm.

01:30:44.523 --> 01:30:47.692
Everyone fails at who
they're supposed to be, Thor.

01:30:48.402 --> 01:30:51.446
The measure of a person,
of a hero...

01:30:51.614 --> 01:30:54.991
is how well they succeed
at being who they are.

01:31:00.247 --> 01:31:01.706
I've really missed you, Mom.

01:31:07.588 --> 01:31:09.339
Thor! I got it!

01:31:10.216 --> 01:31:11.758
ASGARDIAN GUARD:
Get that rabbit!

01:31:14.762 --> 01:31:16.346
Mom, I have to tell you
something.

01:31:16.513 --> 01:31:18.306
No, son, you don't.

01:31:18.474 --> 01:31:20.975
You're here to repair
your future, not mine.

01:31:21.143 --> 01:31:22.810
This is about your future.

01:31:22.895 --> 01:31:24.312
Uh, it's none of my business.

01:31:25.147 --> 01:31:26.439
- (LOUD THUD)
- (ROCKET PANTING)

01:31:28.317 --> 01:31:29.567
Hi.

01:31:29.735 --> 01:31:31.736
You must be Mom.

01:31:31.904 --> 01:31:33.363
I got the thing.
Come on. We gotta move.

01:31:33.530 --> 01:31:34.989
Oh, I wish we had more time.

01:31:35.157 --> 01:31:36.991
No, this was a gift.

01:31:37.159 --> 01:31:40.578
Now you go and be the man
you're meant to be.

01:31:41.038 --> 01:31:43.206
- I love you, Mom.
- I love you.

01:31:47.670 --> 01:31:49.587
And eat a salad.

01:31:50.589 --> 01:31:51.714
Come on, we gotta go.

01:31:51.882 --> 01:31:53.466
- Goodbye.
- ROCKET: Three...

01:31:53.634 --> 01:31:54.717
- Two...
- No, wait!

01:31:57.972 --> 01:31:59.180
What am I looking at?

01:31:59.348 --> 01:32:00.807
Oh, sometimes
it takes a second.

01:32:03.602 --> 01:32:04.602
(GRUNTS)

01:32:05.187 --> 01:32:06.604
(LAUGHS)

01:32:10.276 --> 01:32:12.318
(PANTING) I'm still worthy.

01:32:13.737 --> 01:32:15.363
Oh, boy.

01:32:16.532 --> 01:32:18.449
- Goodbye, Mom.
- (MOUTHS) Goodbye.

01:32:20.411 --> 01:32:22.662
('70s FUNK ROCK SONG PLAYING)

01:32:35.509 --> 01:32:37.135
(LIP-SYNCING TO SONG)

01:32:46.228 --> 01:32:47.228
(SCREECHES)

01:32:47.313 --> 01:32:49.105
(QUILL SINGING ALONG TO SONG)

01:32:57.698 --> 01:32:59.324
So, he's an idiot?

01:33:00.659 --> 01:33:02.076
Yeah.

01:33:10.586 --> 01:33:11.794
RHODES: What's that?

01:33:11.962 --> 01:33:13.838
The tool of a thief.

01:33:21.680 --> 01:33:22.764
RHODES: Whoa, whoa, whoa.

01:33:23.599 --> 01:33:25.224
This is the part
where spikes come out...

01:33:25.392 --> 01:33:26.893
with skeletons on the end
of them and everything.

01:33:26.977 --> 01:33:28.186
What are you talking about?

01:33:28.354 --> 01:33:29.395
When you break into
a place called

01:33:29.480 --> 01:33:30.688
"The Temple
of the Power Stone"...

01:33:30.856 --> 01:33:32.148
there's gonna be
a bunch of booby traps.

01:33:32.316 --> 01:33:34.567
- Oh, my God.
- Okay. All right. Go ahead.

01:33:59.593 --> 01:34:00.635
(BLOWS)

01:34:07.851 --> 01:34:09.352
I wasn't always like this.

01:34:10.270 --> 01:34:11.270
Me either.

01:34:13.065 --> 01:34:14.524
But we work
with what we got, right?

01:34:16.235 --> 01:34:17.318
Hmm.

01:34:18.278 --> 01:34:19.946
Let's sync up.

01:34:21.824 --> 01:34:24.283
Three, two, one.

01:34:27.246 --> 01:34:28.955
(GRUNTING)

01:34:31.959 --> 01:34:33.334
(GROANING)

01:34:35.963 --> 01:34:37.046
(SCREAMING)

01:34:37.131 --> 01:34:38.756
BANNER:
<i>You murdered trillions!</i>

01:34:38.924 --> 01:34:40.216
THANOS:
<i>You should be grateful.</i>

01:34:40.300 --> 01:34:41.509
(BANNER GRUNTS)

01:34:41.969 --> 01:34:43.553
NATASHA:
<i>Where are the stones?</i>

01:34:43.720 --> 01:34:44.720
<i>Gone.</i>

01:34:45.472 --> 01:34:46.472
<i>Reduced to atoms.</i>

01:34:47.182 --> 01:34:48.850
BANNER: You used them
<i>two days ago!</i>

01:34:49.143 --> 01:34:52.145
<i>I used the stones</i>
<i>to destroy the stones.</i>

01:34:52.312 --> 01:34:54.147
<i>It nearly killed me.</i>

01:34:54.314 --> 01:34:56.232
<i>But the work is done.</i>

01:34:56.400 --> 01:34:58.234
<i>It always will be.</i>

01:34:59.528 --> 01:35:02.989
<i>I am inevitable.</i>

01:35:04.241 --> 01:35:06.284
What did you do to them?

01:35:06.452 --> 01:35:07.702
Nothing.

01:35:08.579 --> 01:35:09.871
Yet.

01:35:11.665 --> 01:35:13.583
They're not trying
to stop something

01:35:13.667 --> 01:35:15.376
I'm going to do in our time.

01:35:15.711 --> 01:35:17.712
They're trying
to undo something

01:35:17.796 --> 01:35:19.338
I've already done in theirs.

01:35:19.506 --> 01:35:21.174
The stones.

01:35:22.092 --> 01:35:24.010
I found them all.

01:35:25.804 --> 01:35:27.180
I won.

01:35:27.931 --> 01:35:30.892
Tipped the cosmic scales
to balance.

01:35:34.897 --> 01:35:36.647
This is your future.

01:35:36.982 --> 01:35:39.025
It's my destiny.

01:35:40.235 --> 01:35:42.278
NEBULA:
<i>My father is many things.</i>

01:35:42.446 --> 01:35:44.280
<i>A liar is not one of them.</i>

01:35:45.949 --> 01:35:46.949
<i>Ah.</i>

01:35:47.993 --> 01:35:49.911
<i>Thank you, daughter.</i>

01:35:50.078 --> 01:35:52.246
<i>Perhaps I treated you</i>
<i>too harshly.</i>

01:35:52.581 --> 01:35:53.831
(THOR GRUNTS)

01:35:56.752 --> 01:35:59.629
And that is destiny fulfilled.

01:36:00.047 --> 01:36:01.422
Sire...

01:36:01.590 --> 01:36:02.715
your daughter...

01:36:03.091 --> 01:36:04.383
(CHOKING)

01:36:05.177 --> 01:36:06.177
NEBULA: No!

01:36:06.637 --> 01:36:07.678
...is a traitor.

01:36:07.846 --> 01:36:10.306
That's not me.
It's not, I could never...

01:36:10.474 --> 01:36:11.641
I would never betray you.

01:36:11.808 --> 01:36:13.643
Never. Never.

01:36:19.399 --> 01:36:20.566
THANOS: I know.

01:36:21.527 --> 01:36:24.779
And you'll have the chance
to prove it.

01:36:27.824 --> 01:36:29.033
(MOANS)

01:36:31.078 --> 01:36:32.161
No!

01:36:32.871 --> 01:36:34.080
He knows!

01:36:38.669 --> 01:36:40.711
Barton! Barton, come in.

01:36:41.338 --> 01:36:42.630
Romanoff!

01:36:43.257 --> 01:36:44.674
Come in, we have a problem.

01:36:44.841 --> 01:36:45.967
Come on!

01:36:46.134 --> 01:36:47.552
Come in, we have a...

01:36:47.719 --> 01:36:49.053
Thanos knows.

01:36:49.721 --> 01:36:50.972
Thanos...

01:37:04.695 --> 01:37:05.778
TONY: Cap.

01:37:07.406 --> 01:37:09.657
Sorry, buddy,
we got a problem.

01:37:09.783 --> 01:37:11.826
(SCOFFS) Yeah, we do.

01:37:12.411 --> 01:37:13.494
STEVE: Well,
what are we gonna do now?

01:37:13.579 --> 01:37:14.662
TONY: You know what?
Give me a break, Steve.

01:37:14.746 --> 01:37:16.122
I just got hit in the head
with the Hulk.

01:37:16.206 --> 01:37:17.748
(SCOFFS) You said
that we had one shot.

01:37:17.916 --> 01:37:19.250
This was our shot.

01:37:19.418 --> 01:37:21.419
We shot it. It's shot.
Six stones or nothing.

01:37:21.587 --> 01:37:23.045
- It was six stones or nothing.
- You're repeating yourself,

01:37:23.130 --> 01:37:24.130
you know that?
You're repeating yourself.

01:37:24.298 --> 01:37:25.965
You're repeating yourself.
You're repeating yourself.

01:37:26.049 --> 01:37:27.049
Dude. Come on!

01:37:27.134 --> 01:37:28.134
No. You never wanted
a time heist.

01:37:28.218 --> 01:37:29.218
You weren't on board
with the time heist.

01:37:29.303 --> 01:37:30.511
- I dropped the ball.
- You ruined the time heist.

01:37:30.596 --> 01:37:31.971
TONY: Is that what I did?
SCOTT: Yeah.

01:37:32.055 --> 01:37:33.848
Are there any other options
with the Tesseract?

01:37:34.016 --> 01:37:35.224
No, no, no,
there's no other options.

01:37:35.392 --> 01:37:36.642
There's no do-overs.

01:37:36.810 --> 01:37:38.853
We're not going anywhere else.
We have one particle left.

01:37:38.937 --> 01:37:39.937
Each.

01:37:40.063 --> 01:37:42.356
That's it. All right?
We use that...

01:37:42.524 --> 01:37:43.691
bye-bye,
you're not going home.

01:37:43.859 --> 01:37:45.818
Yeah, well, if we don't try...

01:37:45.986 --> 01:37:47.153
then no one else
is going home, either.

01:37:47.321 --> 01:37:48.321
I got it.

01:37:49.531 --> 01:37:51.782
There's another way
to retake the Tesseract

01:37:51.867 --> 01:37:53.576
and acquire new particles.

01:37:54.411 --> 01:37:55.453
Little stroll down
memory lane.

01:37:56.246 --> 01:37:58.080
Military installation,
Garden State.

01:38:02.169 --> 01:38:03.461
When were they both there?

01:38:03.629 --> 01:38:06.005
They were there at a time...
I have a vaguely exact idea.

01:38:06.673 --> 01:38:07.673
- How vague?
- SCOTT: What are you

01:38:07.758 --> 01:38:08.799
talking about?
Where are we going?

01:38:08.884 --> 01:38:09.884
TONY: I know for a fact
they were there.

01:38:09.968 --> 01:38:10.968
Who's they? What are we doing?

01:38:11.053 --> 01:38:12.136
And I know how I know.

01:38:14.056 --> 01:38:15.598
SCOTT: Guys, what is it?

01:38:16.183 --> 01:38:17.808
Looks like we're improvising.

01:38:17.976 --> 01:38:19.185
- Great.
- What are we improvising?

01:38:19.269 --> 01:38:21.020
Scott, get this back
to the compound.

01:38:21.188 --> 01:38:22.188
TONY: Suit up.

01:38:22.439 --> 01:38:23.856
- What's in New Jersey?
- TONY: 0-4.

01:38:23.940 --> 01:38:24.940
0-4.

01:38:25.067 --> 01:38:26.150
- TONY: Uh, 0-7.
- 0-7.

01:38:26.234 --> 01:38:28.110
- Excuse me.
- 1 -9-7-0.

01:38:28.570 --> 01:38:29.570
Are you sure?

01:38:29.655 --> 01:38:30.946
SCOTT: Cap? Captain?

01:38:31.114 --> 01:38:32.948
Steve? Sorry.

01:38:33.116 --> 01:38:34.742
America. Rogers.

01:38:34.910 --> 01:38:36.118
Look, if you do this...

01:38:36.411 --> 01:38:38.954
and it doesn't work,
you're not coming back.

01:38:40.040 --> 01:38:41.832
Thanks for the pep talk,
pissant.

01:38:42.876 --> 01:38:44.085
You trust me?

01:38:44.961 --> 01:38:46.128
I do.

01:38:47.172 --> 01:38:48.506
Your call.

01:38:49.383 --> 01:38:51.092
Here we go.

01:38:56.098 --> 01:38:57.723
('70s ROCK SONG PLAYING)

01:39:07.150 --> 01:39:10.778
Hey, man!
Make love, not war.

01:39:16.702 --> 01:39:19.370
TONY: Clearly you weren't
actually born here, right?

01:39:19.538 --> 01:39:21.038
STEVE: The idea of me was.

01:39:22.207 --> 01:39:23.749
TONY: Right. Well,
imagine you're S.H.I.E.L.D...

01:39:23.917 --> 01:39:27.169
running a quasi-fascistic
intelligence organization...

01:39:28.505 --> 01:39:30.089
where do you hide it?

01:39:30.257 --> 01:39:31.924
In plain sight.

01:39:40.142 --> 01:39:41.225
(VISOR TRILLS)

01:39:57.451 --> 01:39:58.576
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

01:40:00.328 --> 01:40:01.454
Good luck
on your mission, Captain.

01:40:01.621 --> 01:40:04.165
Good luck
on your project, Doctor.

01:40:07.586 --> 01:40:08.669
You new here?

01:40:11.214 --> 01:40:12.548
Not exactly.

01:40:19.264 --> 01:40:21.056
Come on, you bastard.

01:40:27.856 --> 01:40:29.356
Gotcha.

01:40:34.237 --> 01:40:35.237
Whew.

01:40:45.290 --> 01:40:46.499
(SIGHS)

01:40:46.875 --> 01:40:48.542
Back in the game.

01:40:51.213 --> 01:40:52.421
HOWARD: Arnim, you in there?

01:40:53.381 --> 01:40:54.423
Arnim?

01:40:59.721 --> 01:41:01.055
Hey!

01:41:01.723 --> 01:41:03.432
The door is this way, pal.

01:41:04.267 --> 01:41:05.309
Oh, yeah.

01:41:05.477 --> 01:41:07.353
Looking for Doctor Zola,
have you seen him?

01:41:07.521 --> 01:41:10.940
Yeah, Doctor Zola.
No, I haven't seen a soul.

01:41:12.442 --> 01:41:13.776
Pardon me.

01:41:14.528 --> 01:41:16.153
Do I know you?

01:41:17.405 --> 01:41:18.405
No, sir. Uh...

01:41:19.866 --> 01:41:21.659
I'm a visitor from MIT.

01:41:22.244 --> 01:41:23.369
Oh. MIT.

01:41:23.829 --> 01:41:24.954
Got a name?

01:41:25.413 --> 01:41:26.539
Howard.

01:41:26.706 --> 01:41:29.208
- That'll be easy to remember.
- Howard...

01:41:30.210 --> 01:41:31.210
Potts.

01:41:31.795 --> 01:41:34.004
Well, I'm Howard Stark.

01:41:34.172 --> 01:41:35.172
Hi.

01:41:35.257 --> 01:41:36.549
Shake that, don't pull it.

01:41:36.716 --> 01:41:37.716
Yeah.

01:41:39.135 --> 01:41:41.345
You look a little green around
the gills, there, Potts.

01:41:41.513 --> 01:41:43.681
I'm fine. Just long hours.

01:41:43.849 --> 01:41:45.558
You wanna get some air?

01:41:48.103 --> 01:41:49.895
- Hello, Potts.
- Yeah.

01:41:50.063 --> 01:41:51.313
- That'd be swell.
- That way.

01:41:51.481 --> 01:41:52.481
Okay.

01:41:52.607 --> 01:41:54.275
Need your briefcase?

01:41:56.862 --> 01:41:58.112
(CHUCKLES)

01:41:58.613 --> 01:42:01.198
You're not one of those
beatniks, are you, Potts?

01:42:03.702 --> 01:42:05.244
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

01:42:07.038 --> 01:42:08.831
HANK PYM: Hello?
STEVE: (ON PHONE) Doctor Pym?

01:42:08.999 --> 01:42:11.208
HANK PYM: That would be the
number that you called, yes.

01:42:11.376 --> 01:42:13.627
<i>This is Captain Stevens</i>
<i>from shipping.</i>

01:42:13.795 --> 01:42:14.920
<i>We have a package for you.</i>

01:42:15.005 --> 01:42:16.463
Oh, bring it up.

01:42:16.631 --> 01:42:18.591
<i>That's the thing, sir,</i>
<i>we can't.</i>

01:42:19.718 --> 01:42:22.344
I'm confused.
I thought that was your job.

01:42:22.512 --> 01:42:23.888
<i>Well, it's just...</i>

01:42:24.055 --> 01:42:25.514
<i>Sir, the box is glowing...</i>

01:42:25.682 --> 01:42:26.682
<i>and to be honest,</i>

01:42:26.766 --> 01:42:28.475
<i>some of our mail guys</i>
<i>aren't feeling that great.</i>

01:42:28.643 --> 01:42:30.352
They didn't open it, did they?

01:42:30.520 --> 01:42:32.688
<i>Uh, yeah, they did.</i>
<i>You better get down here.</i>

01:42:33.523 --> 01:42:35.441
Excuse me!
Out of the way!

01:43:02.636 --> 01:43:06.138
So, flowers and sauerkraut.
You got a big date tonight?

01:43:06.890 --> 01:43:08.349
Uh, my wife's expecting.

01:43:08.516 --> 01:43:11.352
And too much time
at the office.

01:43:13.188 --> 01:43:14.563
Congratulations.

01:43:14.731 --> 01:43:16.857
- Thanks. Hold this, will ya?
- Yeah, sure.

01:43:17.943 --> 01:43:20.027
- How far along is she?
- Uh, I don't know.

01:43:21.821 --> 01:43:22.947
She's at the point where

01:43:23.031 --> 01:43:24.573
she can't stand
the sound of my chewing.

01:43:24.741 --> 01:43:28.202
I guess I'll be eating dinner
in the pantry again.

01:43:29.120 --> 01:43:30.120
I have a little girl.

01:43:30.288 --> 01:43:31.789
A girl would be nice.

01:43:31.957 --> 01:43:33.958
Less of a chance she'd
turn out exactly like me.

01:43:34.626 --> 01:43:36.085
What'd be so awful about that?

01:43:36.252 --> 01:43:38.253
Let's just say
that the greater good

01:43:38.338 --> 01:43:41.632
has rarely outweighed
my own self-interest.

01:43:45.679 --> 01:43:46.845
GUARD: And you've never seen
these two men before?

01:43:46.930 --> 01:43:48.722
No, I've got an eye for this.
The two of them looked fishy.

01:43:48.890 --> 01:43:49.890
Can you describe them?

01:43:49.975 --> 01:43:51.141
One of them
had a hippie beard.

01:43:51.309 --> 01:43:53.477
GUARD: Hippie.
Like Bee Gees or Mungo Jerry?

01:43:53.645 --> 01:43:54.687
FEMALE AGENT:
Definitely Mungo Jerry.

01:43:54.854 --> 01:43:55.854
Yeah, this is Chesler.

01:43:55.939 --> 01:43:57.106
I need every available MP
to sublevel six.

01:43:57.190 --> 01:43:59.066
We have a potential breach.

01:44:16.960 --> 01:44:17.960
PEGGY: I said bring them in.

01:44:18.086 --> 01:44:19.128
They're trying, ma'am,
but Braddock's unit

01:44:19.212 --> 01:44:20.212
has been stopped
by lightning strikes.

01:44:20.296 --> 01:44:21.338
Oh, for the love of...

01:44:21.423 --> 01:44:22.923
I'll look at
the weather projections.

01:44:24.300 --> 01:44:25.300
(INDISTINCT)

01:44:46.948 --> 01:44:48.949
It's not lightning strikes
we're looking at.

01:45:00.295 --> 01:45:02.004
TONY: So, where you at
with names?

01:45:02.172 --> 01:45:05.299
HOWARD: Well, if it's a boy,
my wife likes Elmonzo.

01:45:05.467 --> 01:45:07.426
TONY: Huh. Might wanna
let that stew awhile.

01:45:07.510 --> 01:45:08.969
- You got time.
- Uh-huh.

01:45:10.346 --> 01:45:11.847
Let me ask you a question.

01:45:12.849 --> 01:45:16.101
When your kid was born,
were you nervous?

01:45:16.269 --> 01:45:17.770
- Wildly.
- (SIGHS)

01:45:17.854 --> 01:45:19.563
- Yeah.
- Did you feel qualified?

01:45:19.731 --> 01:45:21.607
Like you had any idea

01:45:21.691 --> 01:45:23.317
how to successfully operate
that thing?

01:45:23.735 --> 01:45:26.570
I literally pieced it together
as I went along.

01:45:26.738 --> 01:45:28.739
I thought about
what my dad did.

01:45:29.199 --> 01:45:30.449
HOWARD: (SIGHS) My old man,

01:45:30.533 --> 01:45:32.326
he never met a problem
he couldn't solve with a belt.

01:45:32.410 --> 01:45:34.453
I thought my dad
was tough on me.

01:45:34.621 --> 01:45:35.954
And now, looking back on it,

01:45:36.039 --> 01:45:37.331
I just remember
the good stuff.

01:45:37.499 --> 01:45:39.083
You know?
He did drop the odd pearl.

01:45:39.250 --> 01:45:40.626
Yeah? Like what?

01:45:41.753 --> 01:45:44.254
"No amount of money
ever bought a second of time."

01:45:45.590 --> 01:45:46.632
Smart guy.

01:45:47.050 --> 01:45:48.509
He did his best.

01:45:49.886 --> 01:45:51.386
I'll tell you,
that kid's not even here yet

01:45:51.471 --> 01:45:53.847
and there's nothing
I wouldn't do for him.

01:46:02.607 --> 01:46:03.982
Good to meet you, Potts.

01:46:04.484 --> 01:46:05.484
Yeah.

01:46:05.902 --> 01:46:07.069
Howard...

01:46:07.654 --> 01:46:09.238
everything's gonna be
all right.

01:46:12.242 --> 01:46:13.492
Thank you...

01:46:14.452 --> 01:46:15.786
for everything...

01:46:16.204 --> 01:46:18.497
you've done for this country.

01:46:21.376 --> 01:46:22.501
HOWARD: Jarvis.

01:46:26.214 --> 01:46:27.756
Have we ever met that guy?

01:46:29.759 --> 01:46:31.260
You meet a lot of people, sir.

01:46:33.888 --> 01:46:35.514
Seems very familiar.

01:46:36.432 --> 01:46:37.891
Weird beard.

01:46:43.982 --> 01:46:45.149
(GRUNTS)

01:46:45.859 --> 01:46:47.234
(PANTING) You're weak.

01:46:47.777 --> 01:46:48.861
I'm you.

01:46:49.571 --> 01:46:50.571
(GROANS)

01:46:53.324 --> 01:46:54.449
(GASPS)

01:47:06.504 --> 01:47:08.589
NEBULA: You could stop this.

01:47:08.882 --> 01:47:10.674
You know you want to.

01:47:11.384 --> 01:47:13.552
Did you see
what happens in the future?

01:47:14.846 --> 01:47:17.222
Thanos finds the Soul Stone.

01:47:18.766 --> 01:47:20.767
You wanna know
how he does that?

01:47:22.145 --> 01:47:26.315
You wanna know
what he does to you?

01:47:26.816 --> 01:47:27.816
That's enough.

01:47:28.318 --> 01:47:29.693
- (GRUNTS)
- (NEBULA GROANS)

01:47:35.241 --> 01:47:36.533
(NEBULA CHOKES)

01:47:40.496 --> 01:47:42.080
You disgust me.

01:47:43.374 --> 01:47:48.253
But that doesn't mean
you're useless.

01:48:09.943 --> 01:48:11.652
How do I look?

01:48:18.243 --> 01:48:19.243
Wow.

01:48:20.245 --> 01:48:23.372
Under different
circumstances...

01:48:23.539 --> 01:48:25.540
this would be totally awesome.

01:48:37.470 --> 01:48:38.845
NATASHA: (GROANS)
I bet the raccoon

01:48:38.930 --> 01:48:40.514
didn't have to climb
a mountain.

01:48:40.682 --> 01:48:42.599
Technically he's not
a raccoon, you know?

01:48:42.684 --> 01:48:44.309
Oh, whatever.
He eats garbage.

01:48:44.477 --> 01:48:45.811
RED SKULL: Welcome.

01:48:48.982 --> 01:48:50.315
Natasha.

01:48:50.483 --> 01:48:51.483
Daughter of Ivan.

01:48:52.819 --> 01:48:53.944
Clint.

01:48:54.112 --> 01:48:56.405
Son of Edith.

01:49:01.786 --> 01:49:03.245
Who are you?

01:49:03.871 --> 01:49:06.331
Consider me a guide...

01:49:06.499 --> 01:49:08.166
to you...

01:49:08.334 --> 01:49:10.168
and to all who seek
the Soul Stone.

01:49:10.336 --> 01:49:11.378
Oh, good.

01:49:11.546 --> 01:49:13.672
You tell us where it is,
then we'll be on our way.

01:49:14.465 --> 01:49:16.091
(SPEAKS GERMAN)

01:49:17.593 --> 01:49:19.845
If only it were that easy.

01:49:31.941 --> 01:49:35.652
What you seek
lies in front of you.

01:49:36.904 --> 01:49:39.323
As does what you fear.

01:49:44.245 --> 01:49:46.121
The stone's down there.

01:49:46.748 --> 01:49:48.665
RED SKULL: For one of you.

01:49:48.958 --> 01:49:50.667
For the other...

01:49:53.338 --> 01:49:55.255
In order to take the stone...

01:49:55.423 --> 01:49:58.425
you must lose
that which you love.

01:49:59.802 --> 01:50:02.971
An everlasting exchange.

01:50:03.973 --> 01:50:08.060
A soul for a soul.

01:50:10.646 --> 01:50:13.231
BARTON: How's it going?
(CHUCKLES)

01:50:15.443 --> 01:50:16.860
Jesus.

01:50:17.195 --> 01:50:18.904
Maybe he's making
this shit up.

01:50:19.781 --> 01:50:21.114
No.

01:50:21.949 --> 01:50:22.949
I don't think so.

01:50:23.659 --> 01:50:25.827
Why? 'Cause he knows
your daddy's name?

01:50:27.330 --> 01:50:28.372
I didn't.

01:50:29.874 --> 01:50:32.250
Thanos left here
with the stone...

01:50:32.919 --> 01:50:34.461
without his daughter.

01:50:34.629 --> 01:50:36.713
That's not a coincidence.

01:50:37.799 --> 01:50:39.424
Yeah.

01:50:41.135 --> 01:50:43.011
Whatever it takes.

01:50:47.517 --> 01:50:49.017
Whatever it takes.

01:50:53.398 --> 01:50:55.357
If we don't get that stone...

01:50:55.525 --> 01:50:57.192
billions of people stay dead.

01:50:58.069 --> 01:50:59.236
Yeah.

01:51:01.114 --> 01:51:03.240
Then I guess we both know
who it's gotta be.

01:51:03.991 --> 01:51:05.158
I guess we do.

01:51:13.584 --> 01:51:15.710
I'm starting to think we mean

01:51:15.795 --> 01:51:18.296
different people here,
Natasha.

01:51:18.798 --> 01:51:20.632
For the last five years, I've
been trying to do one thing.

01:51:20.800 --> 01:51:22.050
Get to right here.

01:51:22.218 --> 01:51:24.219
That's all it's been about.
Bringing everybody back.

01:51:24.387 --> 01:51:26.596
No, don't you get
all decent on me now.

01:51:26.764 --> 01:51:28.765
What, you think I wanna do it?

01:51:29.350 --> 01:51:31.101
I'm trying to save your life,
you idiot.

01:51:31.269 --> 01:51:33.603
Yeah, well, I don't
want you to. How's that?

01:51:34.522 --> 01:51:36.731
Natasha, you know
what I've done.

01:51:38.401 --> 01:51:40.193
You know what I've become.

01:51:42.321 --> 01:51:44.906
Oh, I don't judge people
on their worst mistakes.

01:51:49.078 --> 01:51:50.328
Maybe you should.

01:51:51.205 --> 01:51:52.747
You didn't.

01:51:58.921 --> 01:52:01.131
You're a pain in my ass,
you know that?

01:52:12.226 --> 01:52:13.435
Okay.

01:52:15.188 --> 01:52:16.688
You win.

01:52:20.318 --> 01:52:21.818
(GRUNTING)

01:52:23.154 --> 01:52:24.321
Tell my family I love 'em.

01:52:25.490 --> 01:52:26.615
(GRUNTING)

01:52:28.034 --> 01:52:29.242
You tell 'em yourself.

01:52:29.494 --> 01:52:30.494
(GROANS)

01:52:37.793 --> 01:52:38.835
(GRUNTS)

01:52:55.853 --> 01:52:57.229
(BOTH GRUNTING)

01:53:02.109 --> 01:53:03.109
Damn you.

01:53:08.950 --> 01:53:09.950
(GRUNTS)

01:53:10.618 --> 01:53:11.618
Wait.

01:53:19.669 --> 01:53:21.503
Let me go.

01:53:22.755 --> 01:53:23.755
No.

01:53:25.508 --> 01:53:26.508
No. Please, no.

01:53:29.887 --> 01:53:31.721
It's okay.

01:53:33.766 --> 01:53:34.766
Please.

01:53:36.852 --> 01:53:37.852
No!

01:54:38.164 --> 01:54:40.248
(PANTING)

01:54:53.721 --> 01:54:55.055
(SOBBING)

01:55:19.330 --> 01:55:20.330
Did we get 'em all?

01:55:21.749 --> 01:55:23.541
Are you telling me
this actually worked?

01:55:28.381 --> 01:55:29.589
Clint, where's Nat?

01:55:36.597 --> 01:55:37.722
(GASPS SOFTLY)

01:55:58.828 --> 01:55:59.828
Do we know if she had family?

01:56:00.996 --> 01:56:02.163
Yeah.

01:56:02.331 --> 01:56:03.331
Us.

01:56:04.750 --> 01:56:05.792
What?

01:56:06.669 --> 01:56:07.669
Huh?

01:56:07.753 --> 01:56:09.003
- What are you doing?
- Just asked him a question.

01:56:09.088 --> 01:56:10.338
Yeah, no, you're acting
like she's dead.

01:56:10.506 --> 01:56:11.631
Why are we acting
like she's dead?

01:56:11.716 --> 01:56:12.966
We have the stones, right?

01:56:13.134 --> 01:56:14.134
As long as we have
the stones...

01:56:14.301 --> 01:56:16.052
Cap, we can bring her back.
Isn't that right?

01:56:16.220 --> 01:56:18.221
So, stop this shit. We're the
Avengers. Get it together.

01:56:18.389 --> 01:56:19.597
Can't get her back.

01:56:22.601 --> 01:56:23.852
What's he...?
What?

01:56:24.019 --> 01:56:25.228
It can't be undone.

01:56:25.813 --> 01:56:27.522
It can't.

01:56:28.190 --> 01:56:29.524
(LAUGHS)

01:56:30.025 --> 01:56:31.401
Look, I'm sorry, no offense,

01:56:31.485 --> 01:56:33.153
but you're a very
earthly being, okay?

01:56:33.320 --> 01:56:34.612
And we're talking
about space magic.

01:56:34.780 --> 01:56:36.781
And "can't" seems very
definitive. Don't you think?

01:56:36.949 --> 01:56:38.324
Yeah, look,
I know that I'm way outside

01:56:38.409 --> 01:56:39.784
my pay grade here.

01:56:39.952 --> 01:56:41.411
But she still
isn't here, is she?

01:56:41.579 --> 01:56:42.579
THOR: No, that's my point.

01:56:42.747 --> 01:56:45.707
It can't be undone.

01:56:45.875 --> 01:56:47.292
Or that's at least

01:56:47.376 --> 01:56:49.210
what the red,
floating guy had to say.

01:56:49.378 --> 01:56:50.837
Maybe you wanna go
talk to him, okay?

01:56:51.005 --> 01:56:54.048
Go grab your hammer and you
go fly and you talk to him.

01:57:02.600 --> 01:57:04.642
It was supposed to be me.

01:57:06.896 --> 01:57:09.189
She sacrificed her life
for that goddamn stone.

01:57:09.356 --> 01:57:10.815
She bet her life on it.

01:57:11.192 --> 01:57:12.400
(GRUNTS)

01:57:15.738 --> 01:57:18.072
She's not coming back.

01:57:19.867 --> 01:57:21.326
We have to make it worth it.

01:57:21.911 --> 01:57:23.369
We have to.

01:57:24.789 --> 01:57:26.456
We will.

01:57:51.148 --> 01:57:52.273
Boom!

01:57:52.983 --> 01:57:54.943
(CHUCKLES MISCHIEVOUSLY)

01:57:57.947 --> 01:57:59.405
All right, the glove's ready.

01:58:00.199 --> 01:58:02.784
Question is, who's gonna
snap their freakin' fingers?

01:58:02.952 --> 01:58:05.036
- I'll do it.
- TONY: Excuse me?

01:58:05.162 --> 01:58:06.204
THOR: It's okay.

01:58:06.288 --> 01:58:07.288
TONY: Stop, stop. Slow down.

01:58:07.373 --> 01:58:08.873
Thor. Just wait.

01:58:09.041 --> 01:58:10.875
We haven't decided
who's gonna put that on yet.

01:58:11.252 --> 01:58:12.836
I'm sorry. What,
we're all just sitting around

01:58:12.920 --> 01:58:14.170
waiting for
the right opportunity?

01:58:14.338 --> 01:58:15.463
We should at least discuss it.

01:58:15.631 --> 01:58:17.590
Look, sitting here
staring at the thing

01:58:17.675 --> 01:58:19.467
is not gonna bring
everybody back.

01:58:20.511 --> 01:58:22.011
I'm the strongest Avenger,
okay?

01:58:22.096 --> 01:58:23.429
So, this responsibility
falls upon me.

01:58:23.597 --> 01:58:24.806
- Normally, you're right.
- It's my duty.

01:58:24.974 --> 01:58:26.766
- It's not about that.
- It's not that. (SHUSHES)

01:58:26.934 --> 01:58:28.726
- TONY: Hey, buddy...
- Stop it! Just let me.

01:58:31.730 --> 01:58:33.231
Just let me do it.

01:58:33.399 --> 01:58:35.900
Just let me do something good.
Something right.

01:58:36.068 --> 01:58:37.068
Look, it's not
just the fact...

01:58:37.236 --> 01:58:38.361
that that glove is channeling
enough energy

01:58:38.445 --> 01:58:39.362
to light up a continent.

01:58:39.530 --> 01:58:41.531
I'm telling you.
You're in no condition.

01:58:41.699 --> 01:58:44.742
What do you think is coursing
through my veins right now?

01:58:44.910 --> 01:58:45.952
Cheez Whiz?

01:58:48.497 --> 01:58:49.497
Lightning.

01:58:49.665 --> 01:58:50.790
- Yeah.
- Lightning.

01:58:50.958 --> 01:58:52.333
SMART HULK:
Lightning won't help you, pal.

01:58:52.501 --> 01:58:54.335
It's gotta be me.

01:58:55.671 --> 01:58:57.839
You saw what those stones
did to Thanos.

01:58:58.007 --> 01:58:59.549
They almost killed him.

01:59:00.968 --> 01:59:02.844
None of you could survive.

01:59:03.554 --> 01:59:05.179
STEVE: How do we know
you will?

01:59:05.347 --> 01:59:06.389
SMART HULK: We don't.

01:59:06.682 --> 01:59:09.225
But the radiation's
mostly gamma.

01:59:12.730 --> 01:59:14.314
It's like...

01:59:16.191 --> 01:59:18.109
I was made for this.

01:59:37.046 --> 01:59:38.546
Good to go, yeah?

01:59:40.674 --> 01:59:41.674
Let's do it.

01:59:41.842 --> 01:59:43.217
Okay, remember,

01:59:43.302 --> 01:59:44.886
everyone Thanos snapped away
five years ago...

01:59:45.054 --> 01:59:47.513
you're just bringing them
back to now, today.

01:59:47.681 --> 01:59:49.098
Don't change anything
from the last five years.

01:59:50.517 --> 01:59:51.684
Got it.

02:00:08.077 --> 02:00:09.327
IRON MAN:
<i>Friday, do me a favor</i>

02:00:09.411 --> 02:00:10.870
<i>and activate</i>
<i>Barn Door Protocol, will ya?</i>

02:00:11.038 --> 02:00:12.330
FRIDAY: Yes, boss.

02:00:20.923 --> 02:00:22.757
Everybody comes home.

02:00:33.519 --> 02:00:35.812
(GROANING)

02:00:46.156 --> 02:00:47.573
Take it off! Take it off!

02:00:47.741 --> 02:00:48.866
No, wait.
Bruce, are you okay?

02:00:48.951 --> 02:00:51.244
- (CONTINUES GROANING)
- IRON MAN: Talk to me, Banner.

02:00:54.415 --> 02:00:55.415
I'm okay.

02:00:55.916 --> 02:00:57.208
I'm okay.

02:01:14.727 --> 02:01:16.144
(PANTING HEAVILY)

02:01:19.314 --> 02:01:20.898
(YELLING)

02:01:25.112 --> 02:01:26.112
(SNAPS)

02:01:28.657 --> 02:01:29.782
STEVE: Bruce!

02:01:31.535 --> 02:01:33.119
Don't move him.

02:01:35.164 --> 02:01:36.706
(GROANING)

02:01:37.958 --> 02:01:39.917
(DOORS OPENING)

02:01:40.002 --> 02:01:42.003
- Did it work?
- We're not sure. It's okay.

02:01:54.558 --> 02:01:56.184
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

02:02:04.943 --> 02:02:06.277
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

02:02:21.710 --> 02:02:23.711
(CELL PHONE
CONTINUES VIBRATING)

02:02:28.509 --> 02:02:29.383
Honey.

02:02:29.551 --> 02:02:30.510
LAURA: Clint?

02:02:30.677 --> 02:02:31.928
Honey.

02:02:32.763 --> 02:02:34.097
Guys...

02:02:36.558 --> 02:02:37.934
I think it worked.

02:02:53.325 --> 02:02:54.700
(WAR MACHINE YELPING)

02:03:20.561 --> 02:03:22.436
I can't breathe!
I can't breathe!

02:03:22.521 --> 02:03:23.604
- (GROANS)
- (RAPID BEEPING)

02:03:23.689 --> 02:03:25.481
Canopy, canopy, canopy.

02:03:29.778 --> 02:03:31.362
(GRUNTING)

02:03:32.114 --> 02:03:33.906
Rhodey, Rocket,
get out of here.

02:03:35.075 --> 02:03:36.617
ROCKET: Let me up! Let me up!

02:03:37.369 --> 02:03:38.119
Come on!

02:03:40.539 --> 02:03:41.998
(RHODES STRAINING)

02:03:45.419 --> 02:03:46.586
(EXHALES)

02:03:48.255 --> 02:03:49.088
Rhodey!

02:03:50.883 --> 02:03:52.008
ROCKET: Huh?

02:03:57.639 --> 02:03:59.348
<i>RHODES: Mayday, Mayday!</i>
<i>Does anybody copy?</i>

02:03:59.433 --> 02:04:00.683
<i>We're on the lower level.</i>
<i>It's flooding!</i>

02:04:00.851 --> 02:04:02.560
ANT-MAN: What? What?

02:04:02.728 --> 02:04:04.896
RHODES: We are drowning!
<i>Does anybody copy? Mayday!</i>

02:04:05.063 --> 02:04:07.231
ANT-MAN: Wait! I'm here!

02:04:07.399 --> 02:04:08.900
I'm here. Can you hear me?

02:04:11.445 --> 02:04:13.029
(GRUNTING)

02:04:15.991 --> 02:04:17.033
(GROANS)

02:04:28.545 --> 02:04:29.754
Cap?

02:04:40.015 --> 02:04:41.807
(QUIET GROWL)

02:04:53.737 --> 02:04:54.862
Okay.

02:04:58.283 --> 02:04:59.784
(CREATURES SNARLING)

02:05:14.132 --> 02:05:15.258
Daughter.

02:05:15.425 --> 02:05:16.592
Yes, Father.

02:05:18.470 --> 02:05:20.179
So, this is the future.

02:05:20.847 --> 02:05:21.681
Well done.

02:05:22.599 --> 02:05:24.100
Thank you, Father.

02:05:24.268 --> 02:05:25.643
They suspected nothing.

02:05:27.980 --> 02:05:29.438
The arrogant never do.

02:05:32.401 --> 02:05:33.526
Go.

02:05:34.486 --> 02:05:36.904
Find the stones,
bring them to me.

02:05:37.072 --> 02:05:38.781
What will you do?

02:05:40.117 --> 02:05:41.784
Wait.

02:05:55.590 --> 02:05:56.882
(WHIRRING)

02:06:07.019 --> 02:06:08.686
Tell me something.

02:06:09.813 --> 02:06:12.231
In the future...

02:06:12.399 --> 02:06:14.275
what happens to you and me?

02:06:16.570 --> 02:06:18.195
I try to kill you.

02:06:19.906 --> 02:06:21.407
Several times.

02:06:22.492 --> 02:06:24.452
But eventually...

02:06:24.619 --> 02:06:26.579
we become friends.

02:06:28.081 --> 02:06:29.790
We become sisters.

02:06:37.466 --> 02:06:38.674
GAMORA: Come on.

02:06:40.719 --> 02:06:42.511
We can stop him.

02:06:50.604 --> 02:06:51.937
TONY: Come on, buddy,
wake up!

02:06:52.022 --> 02:06:53.939
- (GASPING)
- That's my man.

02:06:54.858 --> 02:06:56.901
You lose this again,
I'm keeping it.

02:07:00.447 --> 02:07:01.614
What happened?

02:07:01.782 --> 02:07:03.908
You mess with time,
it tends to mess back.

02:07:04.076 --> 02:07:04.950
You'll see.

02:07:05.827 --> 02:07:06.827
(GRUNTS)

02:07:27.057 --> 02:07:28.432
What's he been doing?

02:07:30.352 --> 02:07:31.769
Absolutely nothing.

02:07:33.522 --> 02:07:35.398
STEVE: Where are the stones?

02:07:35.774 --> 02:07:37.608
Somewhere under all this.

02:07:38.985 --> 02:07:41.195
All I know is
he doesn't have 'em.

02:07:41.363 --> 02:07:43.114
So, we keep it that way.

02:07:43.281 --> 02:07:44.657
You know it's a trap, right?

02:07:44.825 --> 02:07:46.158
Yeah.

02:07:46.326 --> 02:07:47.660
I don't much care.

02:07:48.412 --> 02:07:49.412
Good.

02:07:50.372 --> 02:07:52.873
Just as long
as we're all in agreement.

02:07:52.958 --> 02:07:54.834
(THUNDER CRACKING)

02:08:02.634 --> 02:08:04.635
Let's kill him
properly this time.

02:08:14.020 --> 02:08:16.939
You could not live
with your own failure.

02:08:18.442 --> 02:08:20.276
Where did that bring you?

02:08:23.238 --> 02:08:25.114
Back to me.

02:08:28.535 --> 02:08:31.370
I thought by eliminating
half of life...

02:08:32.122 --> 02:08:34.498
the other half would thrive.

02:08:34.666 --> 02:08:36.000
But you've shown me...

02:08:37.169 --> 02:08:38.919
that's impossible.

02:08:40.839 --> 02:08:44.133
And as long as there are those
that remember what was...

02:08:44.301 --> 02:08:45.801
there will always be those

02:08:45.886 --> 02:08:49.513
that are unable to accept
what can be.

02:08:50.265 --> 02:08:51.515
They will resist.

02:08:52.017 --> 02:08:53.934
Yep, we're all kinds
of stubborn.

02:08:54.853 --> 02:08:56.437
I'm thankful.

02:08:58.607 --> 02:09:00.357
Because now...

02:09:00.525 --> 02:09:02.651
I know what I must do.

02:09:03.111 --> 02:09:06.071
I will shred this universe...

02:09:06.239 --> 02:09:08.282
down to its last atom.

02:09:09.075 --> 02:09:10.743
And then...

02:09:10.911 --> 02:09:13.245
with the stones
you've collected for me...

02:09:14.039 --> 02:09:16.165
create a new one...

02:09:16.333 --> 02:09:18.542
teeming with life...

02:09:18.710 --> 02:09:20.586
that knows not
what it has lost...

02:09:20.754 --> 02:09:23.130
but only
what it has been given.

02:09:26.218 --> 02:09:27.635
A grateful universe.

02:09:28.178 --> 02:09:29.595
Born out of blood.

02:09:29.763 --> 02:09:31.430
They'll never know it.

02:09:32.641 --> 02:09:35.559
Because you won't be alive
to tell them.

02:09:36.937 --> 02:09:38.062
(YELLING)

02:09:48.156 --> 02:09:49.365
(GRUNTING)

02:09:50.158 --> 02:09:51.450
See you
on the other side, man.

02:09:51.535 --> 02:09:52.910
(ROCKET WHIMPERING)

02:09:53.787 --> 02:09:55.788
ANT-MAN: Hang on! I'm coming!

02:09:56.248 --> 02:09:57.414
(GRUNTING)

02:10:04.339 --> 02:10:05.506
(CREATURES SNARLING)

02:10:10.387 --> 02:10:11.720
(BEEPING)

02:10:15.016 --> 02:10:16.183
(GRUNTS)

02:10:16.643 --> 02:10:17.893
(GROWLING)

02:10:26.069 --> 02:10:27.069
Yeah!

02:10:31.283 --> 02:10:32.408
(YELLS)

02:10:34.327 --> 02:10:35.411
(GRUNTS)

02:10:36.538 --> 02:10:38.330
(PANTING)

02:10:41.960 --> 02:10:43.502
Oh, hey.

02:10:43.670 --> 02:10:45.379
I know you.

02:10:48.300 --> 02:10:49.300
Father...

02:10:50.051 --> 02:10:51.468
I have the stones.

02:10:51.636 --> 02:10:52.553
What?

02:10:53.930 --> 02:10:54.847
GAMORA: Stop.

02:11:00.061 --> 02:11:01.478
You're betraying us?

02:11:07.485 --> 02:11:08.777
You don't have to do this.

02:11:11.615 --> 02:11:14.116
I am this.

02:11:14.284 --> 02:11:16.201
No, you're not.

02:11:16.661 --> 02:11:18.537
You've seen what we become.

02:11:24.628 --> 02:11:26.837
Nebula, listen to her.

02:11:28.298 --> 02:11:29.173
You can change.

02:11:35.847 --> 02:11:37.348
He won't let me.

02:11:38.975 --> 02:11:39.725
No!

02:11:40.977 --> 02:11:42.186
(GROANS)

02:11:59.371 --> 02:12:00.746
Okay, Thor. Hit me.

02:12:01.581 --> 02:12:03.082
(YELLING)

02:12:07.128 --> 02:12:08.337
(GRUNTS)

02:12:17.389 --> 02:12:18.681
<i>FRIDAY: Boss, wake up!</i>

02:12:26.898 --> 02:12:28.065
(THOR GRUNTS)

02:12:31.778 --> 02:12:33.529
(BOTH GRUNTING)

02:12:52.465 --> 02:12:53.716
(GRUNTS)

02:13:09.983 --> 02:13:11.275
I knew it!

02:13:20.994 --> 02:13:21.994
(GRUNTS)

02:13:26.374 --> 02:13:27.374
(THANOS GROANING)

02:13:29.127 --> 02:13:30.419
(GRUNTS)

02:13:34.424 --> 02:13:35.424
(GRUNTING)

02:13:39.888 --> 02:13:40.888
(GRUNTS)

02:13:48.146 --> 02:13:48.979
(PANTING)

02:13:50.231 --> 02:13:51.398
(THANOS YELLS)

02:14:08.625 --> 02:14:10.292
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

02:14:26.142 --> 02:14:29.144
(STRAINING)

02:14:33.650 --> 02:14:36.485
In all my years of conquest...

02:14:37.779 --> 02:14:39.530
violence...

02:14:40.573 --> 02:14:42.533
slaughter...

02:14:43.660 --> 02:14:46.078
it was never personal.

02:14:48.665 --> 02:14:50.749
But I'll tell you now...

02:14:52.752 --> 02:14:56.547
what I'm about to do
to your stubborn,

02:14:56.631 --> 02:14:59.007
annoying little planet...

02:15:00.760 --> 02:15:02.970
I'm gonna enjoy it...

02:15:03.888 --> 02:15:06.265
very, very much.

02:15:30.373 --> 02:15:31.665
(INHALES SHARPLY)

02:15:32.041 --> 02:15:33.584
(STRAINED GRUNTING)

02:15:39.799 --> 02:15:41.341
(PANTING)

02:15:48.308 --> 02:15:49.433
(GRUNTS)

02:16:09.746 --> 02:16:11.288
SAM: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>Hey, Cap, you read me?</i>

02:16:17.295 --> 02:16:19.588
<i>Cap, it's Sam.</i>
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

02:16:23.593 --> 02:16:25.010
<i>On your left.</i>

02:17:19.357 --> 02:17:21.775
(ALL CHANTING IN XHOSA)

02:17:50.680 --> 02:17:51.972
Is that everyone?

02:17:52.140 --> 02:17:54.349
What? You wanted more?

02:18:07.280 --> 02:18:09.239
(ALL SHOUTING IN UNISON)

02:18:20.877 --> 02:18:22.836
CAPTAIN AMERICA: Avengers...

02:18:27.967 --> 02:18:29.051
assemble.

02:18:29.135 --> 02:18:30.677
(ALL YELLING)

02:18:51.199 --> 02:18:52.532
(THOR YELLING)

02:19:00.374 --> 02:19:02.084
(ALL SHOUTING)

02:19:04.253 --> 02:19:05.504
M'BAKU: Die!

02:19:09.217 --> 02:19:10.926
(ALL GRUNTING)

02:19:12.678 --> 02:19:14.096
(DRAX YELLING)

02:19:26.150 --> 02:19:28.902
No, no, give me that.
You have the little one.

02:19:42.583 --> 02:19:43.416
SPIDER-MAN: Hey!

02:19:44.418 --> 02:19:45.418
Holy cow!

02:19:45.586 --> 02:19:46.962
You will not believe
what's been going on.

02:19:47.046 --> 02:19:48.255
Do you remember
when we were in space?

02:19:48.422 --> 02:19:49.798
And I got all dusty?

02:19:49.966 --> 02:19:51.049
And I must've passed out,

02:19:51.134 --> 02:19:52.634
because I woke up
and you were gone.

02:19:52.802 --> 02:19:54.427
But Doctor Strange was there,
right? And he was like...

02:19:54.595 --> 02:19:56.096
"It's been five years.
Come on, they need us."

02:19:56.264 --> 02:19:57.848
And then he started doing
the yellow sparkly thing

02:19:57.932 --> 02:19:58.932
- that he does all the time.
- He did? Oh, no.

02:19:59.100 --> 02:20:01.434
What are you doing?
Oh.

02:20:05.439 --> 02:20:06.940
Oh, this is nice.

02:20:21.038 --> 02:20:22.789
(QUILL PANTING)

02:20:28.713 --> 02:20:29.713
Gamora?

02:20:39.140 --> 02:20:40.807
I thought I lost you.

02:20:44.228 --> 02:20:45.312
Ow.

02:20:45.396 --> 02:20:48.315
- (GROANING)
- Don't touch me!

02:20:51.319 --> 02:20:53.153
You missed the first time.

02:20:53.321 --> 02:20:55.322
Then you got 'em
both the second time.

02:20:57.325 --> 02:20:58.408
GAMORA: This is the one?

02:20:58.576 --> 02:20:59.576
Seriously?

02:20:59.744 --> 02:21:01.745
Your choices were him
or a tree.

02:21:02.038 --> 02:21:03.455
(MOUTHING)

02:21:04.081 --> 02:21:05.498
(CREATURE ROARS)

02:21:09.712 --> 02:21:10.837
(YELLING)

02:21:12.548 --> 02:21:13.548
Cap!

02:21:13.716 --> 02:21:15.467
What do you want me to do
with this damn thing?

02:21:18.179 --> 02:21:20.222
Get those stones
as far away as possible!

02:21:20.389 --> 02:21:21.431
SMART HULK: No!

02:21:22.600 --> 02:21:24.559
We need to get 'em back
where they came from.

02:21:24.727 --> 02:21:25.727
No way to get 'em back.

02:21:25.811 --> 02:21:27.312
Thanos destroyed
the quantum tunnel.

02:21:27.480 --> 02:21:28.313
ANT-MAN: Hold on!

02:21:30.191 --> 02:21:32.317
That wasn't
our only time machine.

02:21:32.401 --> 02:21:34.402
(HORN PLAYS LA CUCARACHA)

02:21:38.324 --> 02:21:40.242
Anyone see an ugly brown van
out there?

02:21:40.785 --> 02:21:43.870
Yes! But you're not gonna like
where it's parked!

02:21:44.038 --> 02:21:46.164
Scott, how long you need
to get that thing working?

02:21:47.375 --> 02:21:48.541
Uh, maybe 10 minutes.

02:21:48.709 --> 02:21:50.210
Get it started.
We'll get the stones to you.

02:21:50.378 --> 02:21:51.920
We're on it, Cap.

02:22:01.681 --> 02:22:02.806
TONY: Hey.

02:22:02.974 --> 02:22:05.976
You said one out of
14 million, we win, yeah?

02:22:06.894 --> 02:22:07.894
Tell me this is it.

02:22:08.312 --> 02:22:10.188
If I tell you what happens...

02:22:10.356 --> 02:22:11.523
it won't happen.

02:22:15.111 --> 02:22:16.111
You better be right.

02:22:24.537 --> 02:22:25.912
It's a mess back here.

02:22:26.914 --> 02:22:27.914
It's dead.

02:22:29.208 --> 02:22:30.709
- What?
- It's dead.

02:22:30.876 --> 02:22:32.294
I have to hot-wire it.

02:22:35.381 --> 02:22:36.589
Where's Nebula?

02:22:37.717 --> 02:22:39.050
She's not responding.

02:22:39.427 --> 02:22:40.760
Sire...

02:22:42.888 --> 02:22:44.306
(CREATURES SCREECHING)

02:22:45.891 --> 02:22:46.891
(GRUNTS)

02:22:48.728 --> 02:22:49.936
(CREATURES SNARLING)

02:22:50.521 --> 02:22:51.771
BLACK PANTHER: Clint!

02:22:53.816 --> 02:22:54.941
Give it to me.

02:22:59.864 --> 02:23:00.864
(YELLING)

02:23:17.214 --> 02:23:20.592
You took everything from me.

02:23:20.968 --> 02:23:23.303
I don't even know who you are.

02:23:23.471 --> 02:23:25.096
You will.

02:23:38.944 --> 02:23:40.153
(PANTING)

02:23:42.698 --> 02:23:43.907
(GRUNTS)

02:23:45.618 --> 02:23:46.910
(BLACK PANTHER YELPING)

02:23:47.536 --> 02:23:48.495
SPIDER-MAN: I got it!

02:23:51.040 --> 02:23:52.123
Activate Instant Kill.

02:23:56.504 --> 02:23:57.712
(GRUNTS)

02:24:08.557 --> 02:24:09.766
(GRUNTING)

02:24:15.564 --> 02:24:16.898
Rain fire!

02:24:17.608 --> 02:24:19.526
But, sire, our troops!

02:24:19.693 --> 02:24:21.444
Just do it!

02:24:41.590 --> 02:24:43.967
PEPPER: Uh, is anyone else
<i>seeing this?</i>

02:24:57.898 --> 02:24:59.023
SPIDER-MAN: I got this!

02:24:59.275 --> 02:25:01.067
(GRUNTS) I got this.
Okay, I don't got this.

02:25:01.402 --> 02:25:02.569
(OVER SPEAKERS)
<i>Help, somebody help!</i>

02:25:02.736 --> 02:25:04.612
Hey, Queens, heads up!

02:25:14.665 --> 02:25:15.707
Hang on. I got you, kid.

02:25:19.336 --> 02:25:20.503
SPIDER-MAN: Hey!
Nice to meet you...

02:25:20.671 --> 02:25:22.505
Oh, my God!

02:25:25.968 --> 02:25:26.968
(GRUNTS)

02:25:37.396 --> 02:25:38.521
(YELPS)

02:25:42.318 --> 02:25:43.318
(GRUNTS)

02:25:43.652 --> 02:25:44.819
(GROOT GRUNTS)

02:25:45.529 --> 02:25:47.030
(ROCKET YELLING)

02:25:49.325 --> 02:25:50.325
(BOTH GASP)

02:25:58.751 --> 02:26:00.210
What the hell is this?

02:26:01.003 --> 02:26:02.086
Friday,
what are they firing at?

02:26:02.254 --> 02:26:04.130
<i>FRIDAY: Something just</i>
<i>entered the upper atmosphere.</i>

02:26:13.307 --> 02:26:14.682
(POWERING DOWN)

02:26:17.394 --> 02:26:19.562
Oh, yeah!

02:26:37.331 --> 02:26:39.082
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

02:26:39.458 --> 02:26:41.876
Danvers,
we need an assist here.

02:26:46.298 --> 02:26:47.298
(BEEPS)

02:26:50.636 --> 02:26:53.221
Hi, I'm Peter Parker.

02:26:53.847 --> 02:26:55.265
Hey, Peter Parker.

02:26:55.432 --> 02:26:56.599
You got something for me?

02:26:56.684 --> 02:26:57.850
(GRUNTING)

02:27:02.731 --> 02:27:04.816
I don't know how you're gonna
get it through all of that.

02:27:06.485 --> 02:27:07.902
Don't worry.

02:27:08.779 --> 02:27:10.363
She's got help.

02:27:35.514 --> 02:27:36.848
(SCARLET WITCH GRUNTING)

02:28:00.998 --> 02:28:01.998
(GRUNTS)

02:28:20.559 --> 02:28:21.643
(THOR GRUNTING)

02:28:30.736 --> 02:28:31.819
(YELLS)

02:28:34.239 --> 02:28:35.239
(THANOS GRUNTS)

02:28:57.346 --> 02:28:59.013
(YELLING)

02:28:59.264 --> 02:29:00.723
(CAPTAIN MARVEL GRUNTING)

02:29:17.199 --> 02:29:19.283
(YELLS, GRUNTS)

02:29:41.724 --> 02:29:44.100
(GROANING)

02:29:58.157 --> 02:30:01.659
I am inevitable.

02:30:02.619 --> 02:30:03.786
(CLANGS)

02:30:11.128 --> 02:30:12.670
(WHIRRING)

02:30:21.805 --> 02:30:23.347
And I...

02:30:23.432 --> 02:30:24.891
(PANTING)

02:30:25.017 --> 02:30:26.184
am...

02:30:29.897 --> 02:30:31.397
Iron Man.

02:30:31.732 --> 02:30:32.815
(SNAPS)

02:30:32.900 --> 02:30:34.525
(RUMBLING)

02:30:40.282 --> 02:30:41.866
(RUMBLING QUIETS)

02:31:39.174 --> 02:31:40.550
(SIGHS)

02:32:01.363 --> 02:32:02.530
(GRUNTS)

02:32:09.872 --> 02:32:10.913
(EXHALES)

02:32:28.181 --> 02:32:29.515
(PANTING)

02:32:30.100 --> 02:32:31.809
PETER: Mr. Stark?

02:32:32.227 --> 02:32:34.353
Hey! (BREATHING SHAKILY)

02:32:34.479 --> 02:32:37.440
Mr. Stark. Can you hear me?

02:32:37.608 --> 02:32:39.150
It's Peter.

02:32:40.444 --> 02:32:42.069
Hey.

02:32:43.113 --> 02:32:46.157
We won, Mr. Stark.

02:32:47.993 --> 02:32:50.161
We won, Mr. Stark.

02:32:51.788 --> 02:32:54.624
We won!
You did it, sir, you did it.

02:32:55.083 --> 02:32:56.834
(CRYING) I'm sorry.

02:32:57.002 --> 02:32:58.002
Tony.

02:33:11.683 --> 02:33:12.725
Hey.

02:33:12.893 --> 02:33:14.727
(SOFTLY) Hey, Pep.

02:33:19.024 --> 02:33:20.107
Friday?

02:33:20.275 --> 02:33:23.027
FRIDAY:
<i>Life functions critical.</i>

02:33:31.620 --> 02:33:32.620
Tony?

02:33:33.872 --> 02:33:34.956
Look at me.

02:33:36.208 --> 02:33:37.541
(GROANS WEAKLY)

02:33:37.626 --> 02:33:39.543
We're gonna be okay.

02:33:42.839 --> 02:33:44.131
(WHEEZING)

02:33:44.257 --> 02:33:46.133
You can rest now.

02:33:46.760 --> 02:33:47.969
(WHEEZING STOPS)

02:34:31.054 --> 02:34:32.513
(SOBBING)

02:35:20.145 --> 02:35:21.395
(INAUDIBLE)

02:35:31.656 --> 02:35:34.450
<i>TONY: Everybody wants</i>
<i>a happy ending, right?</i>

02:35:34.618 --> 02:35:36.827
<i>But it doesn't</i>
<i>always roll that way.</i>

02:35:38.914 --> 02:35:40.581
<i>Maybe this time.</i>

02:35:42.167 --> 02:35:44.835
<i>I'm hoping</i>
<i>if you play this back...</i>

02:35:46.505 --> 02:35:47.838
<i>it's in celebration.</i>

02:35:49.091 --> 02:35:52.760
<i>I hope families are reunited.</i>
<i>I hope we get it back.</i>

02:35:52.928 --> 02:35:54.512
<i>And something like</i>
<i>a normal version</i>

02:35:54.596 --> 02:35:56.847
<i>of the planet</i>
<i>has been restored.</i>

02:35:57.015 --> 02:35:58.974
<i>If there ever was</i>
<i>such a thing.</i>

02:35:59.559 --> 02:36:02.561
<i>God, what a world.</i>
<i>Universe, now.</i>

02:36:03.522 --> 02:36:05.523
<i>If you told me 10 years ago</i>
<i>that we weren't alone...</i>

02:36:05.690 --> 02:36:07.691
<i>let alone to this extent,</i>
<i>I mean,</i>

02:36:07.776 --> 02:36:09.360
(STAMMERS) I wouldn't have
<i>been surprised...</i>

02:36:09.528 --> 02:36:11.153
<i>but come on, who knew?</i>

02:36:11.321 --> 02:36:14.115
<i>The epic forces</i>
<i>of darkness and light</i>

02:36:14.199 --> 02:36:15.950
<i>that have come into play.</i>

02:36:16.118 --> 02:36:17.827
<i>And for better or worse...</i>

02:36:17.994 --> 02:36:19.662
<i>that's the reality</i>
<i>Morgan's gonna</i>

02:36:19.746 --> 02:36:22.164
<i>have to find a way</i>
<i>to grow up in.</i>

02:36:22.249 --> 02:36:23.499
(WHIRRING)

02:36:25.418 --> 02:36:26.127
<i>So, I thought I'd probably</i>

02:36:26.211 --> 02:36:27.211
<i>better record</i>
<i>a little greeting...</i>

02:36:27.379 --> 02:36:31.006
<i>in the case of an untimely</i>
<i>death. On my part.</i>

02:36:31.174 --> 02:36:34.426
<i>Not that death at any time</i>
<i>isn't untimely.</i>

02:36:35.637 --> 02:36:36.971
<i>This time travel thing</i>
<i>that we're gonna</i>

02:36:37.055 --> 02:36:38.681
<i>try and pull off tomorrow...</i>

02:36:38.849 --> 02:36:39.849
<i>it's got me</i>
<i>scratching my head</i>

02:36:39.933 --> 02:36:41.058
<i>about the survivability</i>
<i>of it all.</i>

02:36:41.226 --> 02:36:42.685
<i>That's the thing.</i>

02:36:44.646 --> 02:36:46.564
<i>Then again,</i>
<i>that's the hero gig, right?</i>

02:36:46.731 --> 02:36:47.815
<i>Part of the journey</i>
<i>is the end.</i>

02:36:49.818 --> 02:36:50.818
<i>What am I even tripping for?</i>

02:36:50.986 --> 02:36:52.069
<i>Everything is gonna work out</i>

02:36:52.154 --> 02:36:55.072
<i>exactly the way</i>
<i>it's supposed to.</i>

02:36:58.577 --> 02:37:00.244
<i>I love you 3,000.</i>

02:37:03.415 --> 02:37:04.498
(GASPS SOFTLY)

02:39:15.171 --> 02:39:17.631
You know,
I wish there was a way

02:39:17.716 --> 02:39:18.924
that I could let her know.

02:39:21.428 --> 02:39:23.554
That we won.

02:39:24.931 --> 02:39:26.640
We did it.

02:39:30.228 --> 02:39:32.021
She knows.

02:39:36.901 --> 02:39:38.986
They both do.

02:39:47.954 --> 02:39:49.038
<i>HAPPY: How you doing, squirt?</i>

02:39:49.205 --> 02:39:50.205
Good.

02:39:50.373 --> 02:39:51.707
- You good?
- Mm-hmm.

02:39:51.875 --> 02:39:54.585
- Good. You hungry?
- Mm-hmm.

02:39:55.003 --> 02:39:56.003
What do you want?

02:39:56.713 --> 02:39:58.130
Cheeseburgers.

02:40:02.927 --> 02:40:05.179
You know,
your dad liked cheeseburgers.

02:40:05.347 --> 02:40:06.764
Okay.

02:40:09.351 --> 02:40:11.602
I'm gonna get you all
the cheeseburgers you want.

02:40:11.770 --> 02:40:12.770
Okay.

02:40:20.737 --> 02:40:22.404
(BIRD CALLING IN DISTANCE)

02:40:24.240 --> 02:40:26.033
(BELL CLANGING IN DISTANCE)

02:40:26.493 --> 02:40:28.035
(FOOTSTEPS RUSTLING)

02:40:29.537 --> 02:40:30.954
VALKYRIE: So...

02:40:31.206 --> 02:40:33.374
when can we expect you back?

02:40:33.708 --> 02:40:34.875
(THOR SMACKS LIPS)

02:40:34.959 --> 02:40:36.794
Um, about that...

02:40:37.045 --> 02:40:39.213
Thor, your people need a king.

02:40:39.381 --> 02:40:41.256
No, they already have one.

02:40:41.633 --> 02:40:42.800
(LAUGHS)

02:40:43.385 --> 02:40:44.385
That's funny.

02:40:49.974 --> 02:40:51.809
Are you being serious?

02:40:55.480 --> 02:40:57.731
It's time for me
to be who I am...

02:40:58.316 --> 02:41:00.901
rather than
who I'm supposed to be.

02:41:02.195 --> 02:41:03.946
But you, you're a leader.

02:41:04.572 --> 02:41:06.281
That's who you are.

02:41:08.785 --> 02:41:10.744
You know, I'd make
a lot of changes around here.

02:41:10.912 --> 02:41:12.413
(CHUCKLES)
I'm counting on it...

02:41:12.580 --> 02:41:14.081
Your Majesty.

02:41:24.217 --> 02:41:25.426
What will you do?

02:41:26.177 --> 02:41:27.594
I'm not sure.

02:41:27.762 --> 02:41:29.805
For the first time
in a thousand years,

02:41:29.889 --> 02:41:31.306
I have no path.

02:41:31.474 --> 02:41:32.891
I do have a ride though.

02:41:33.059 --> 02:41:35.018
Move it or lose it, hairbag.

02:41:35.103 --> 02:41:36.228
(THOR CHUCKLES)

02:41:39.524 --> 02:41:41.066
THOR: Oh, here we are!

02:41:41.526 --> 02:41:43.068
Tree, good to see you.

02:41:46.072 --> 02:41:47.197
(GRUNTS)

02:41:47.657 --> 02:41:50.951
The Asgardians of the Galaxy
back together again.

02:41:51.369 --> 02:41:53.245
Where to first?

02:41:54.372 --> 02:41:55.414
Hey.

02:41:56.040 --> 02:41:58.000
Just so you know,
this is my ship still.

02:41:58.168 --> 02:41:59.168
I'm in charge.

02:41:59.711 --> 02:42:02.254
I know. I know.
Of course you are.

02:42:02.422 --> 02:42:03.964
Of course.

02:42:04.048 --> 02:42:04.923
(BEEPS)

02:42:05.008 --> 02:42:06.508
(DRAX CRUNCHING)

02:42:06.593 --> 02:42:09.136
See, you say, "Of course,"
but then you touch the map.

02:42:09.304 --> 02:42:10.345
It makes you think that maybe

02:42:10.430 --> 02:42:11.805
you didn't realize
I was in charge.

02:42:12.432 --> 02:42:13.765
Quail, that's your own
insecurities in there.

02:42:13.933 --> 02:42:14.933
Quail?

02:42:15.101 --> 02:42:17.352
Okay? I am merely trying to
be of service and assisting.

02:42:17.520 --> 02:42:18.729
Quill.

02:42:18.897 --> 02:42:19.771
That's what I said.

02:42:19.939 --> 02:42:22.316
You should fight one another
for the honor of leadership.

02:42:22.484 --> 02:42:23.859
Sounds fair.

02:42:25.320 --> 02:42:26.528
(QUILL STAMMERS)

02:42:26.613 --> 02:42:28.989
- It's not necessary, okay?
- It's not.

02:42:29.157 --> 02:42:30.157
ROCKET: I got some blasters,

02:42:30.241 --> 02:42:31.533
unless you guys
wanna use knives.

02:42:31.701 --> 02:42:33.911
Oh, yes! Please, use knives.

02:42:34.078 --> 02:42:35.162
Yeah. Knives.

02:42:35.330 --> 02:42:36.872
I am Groot.

02:42:38.208 --> 02:42:39.958
(BOTH LAUGH)

02:42:42.629 --> 02:42:44.004
Not necessary.

02:42:44.172 --> 02:42:45.631
There shall be
no knifing one another.

02:42:45.798 --> 02:42:48.800
Everybody knows
who's in charge.

02:42:49.594 --> 02:42:51.887
(THOR SIGHS, SMACKS LIPS)

02:42:52.388 --> 02:42:53.597
Me.

02:42:54.682 --> 02:42:55.516
Right?

02:42:56.434 --> 02:42:58.644
Yes, you. (LAUGHS)

02:42:58.895 --> 02:43:01.313
Of course! Of course.

02:43:01.481 --> 02:43:03.148
Of course.

02:43:04.901 --> 02:43:06.443
SMART HULK: Remember...

02:43:07.278 --> 02:43:08.487
you have to return the stones

02:43:08.571 --> 02:43:09.571
to the exact moment
you got 'em...

02:43:09.739 --> 02:43:10.739
or you're gonna open up

02:43:10.823 --> 02:43:12.950
a bunch of nasty
alternative realities.

02:43:13.117 --> 02:43:14.117
Don't worry, Bruce.

02:43:14.661 --> 02:43:16.537
Clip all the branches.

02:43:17.080 --> 02:43:18.830
You know, I tried.

02:43:20.124 --> 02:43:22.125
When I had the gauntlet,
the stones,

02:43:22.210 --> 02:43:24.336
I really tried
to bring her back.

02:43:27.632 --> 02:43:29.258
I miss her, man.

02:43:29.634 --> 02:43:30.634
Me too.

02:43:33.221 --> 02:43:34.638
(HELICOPTER WHIRRING)

02:43:34.722 --> 02:43:37.140
SAM: You know, if you want,
I could come with you.

02:43:39.727 --> 02:43:41.186
You're a good man, Sam.

02:43:41.729 --> 02:43:43.272
This one's on me, though.

02:43:47.735 --> 02:43:49.653
Don't do anything stupid
till I get back.

02:43:51.489 --> 02:43:52.739
How can I?

02:43:52.907 --> 02:43:54.700
You're taking
all the stupid with you.

02:44:02.292 --> 02:44:04.084
Gonna miss you, buddy.

02:44:04.460 --> 02:44:05.961
It's gonna be okay, Buck.

02:44:09.799 --> 02:44:11.091
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

02:44:13.344 --> 02:44:15.137
How long is this gonna take?

02:44:15.388 --> 02:44:18.140
For him, as long as he needs.
For us, five seconds.

02:44:23.229 --> 02:44:24.479
You ready, Cap?

02:44:24.647 --> 02:44:27.065
All right, we'll meet you
back here, okay?

02:44:27.734 --> 02:44:28.859
You bet.

02:44:30.361 --> 02:44:31.945
SMART HULK: Going quantum.
Three...

02:44:32.530 --> 02:44:33.363
two...

02:44:34.032 --> 02:44:35.240
one.

02:44:37.118 --> 02:44:39.161
And returning in five...

02:44:39.329 --> 02:44:40.287
four...

02:44:40.455 --> 02:44:42.289
three, two...

02:44:42.457 --> 02:44:43.790
one.

02:44:51.049 --> 02:44:52.049
Where is he?

02:44:52.216 --> 02:44:53.967
I don't know. He blew
right by his time stamp.

02:44:54.135 --> 02:44:55.594
He should be here.

02:45:01.100 --> 02:45:02.017
SAM: Get him back.

02:45:02.185 --> 02:45:03.310
SMART HULK: I'm trying.
SAM: Get him the hell back.

02:45:03.478 --> 02:45:05.354
- Hey, I said I'm trying.
- Sam.

02:45:29.337 --> 02:45:30.921
Go ahead.

02:45:48.898 --> 02:45:49.648
Cap?

02:45:51.984 --> 02:45:53.735
Hi, Sam.

02:45:56.739 --> 02:45:59.783
So, did something go wrong
or did something go right?

02:46:01.911 --> 02:46:05.747
Well, after I put
the stones back, I thought...

02:46:06.874 --> 02:46:08.208
maybe...

02:46:08.710 --> 02:46:13.505
I'll try some of that life
Tony was telling me to get.

02:46:15.508 --> 02:46:17.634
How'd that work out for ya?

02:46:20.138 --> 02:46:21.555
It was beautiful.

02:46:22.890 --> 02:46:24.599
Good. I'm happy for you.

02:46:24.767 --> 02:46:25.809
Truly.

02:46:26.561 --> 02:46:27.853
Thank you.

02:46:29.188 --> 02:46:30.439
Only thing bumming me out...

02:46:30.606 --> 02:46:32.190
is the fact
I have to live in a world

02:46:32.275 --> 02:46:34.192
without Captain America.

02:46:34.777 --> 02:46:35.944
STEVE: Oh.

02:46:37.989 --> 02:46:40.782
That reminds me.

02:46:49.292 --> 02:46:50.500
Try it on.

02:47:16.027 --> 02:47:17.527
How does it feel?

02:47:20.114 --> 02:47:21.823
Like it's someone else's.

02:47:24.869 --> 02:47:26.036
It isn't.

02:47:29.749 --> 02:47:31.124
(SIGHS)

02:47:39.383 --> 02:47:40.967
Thank you.

02:47:42.678 --> 02:47:43.970
I'll do my best.

02:47:49.352 --> 02:47:51.269
That's why it's yours.

02:47:52.980 --> 02:47:54.356
You wanna tell me about her?

02:48:00.947 --> 02:48:02.447
No.

02:48:02.865 --> 02:48:04.991
No, I don't think I will.

02:48:11.040 --> 02:48:13.208
(OLD JAZZ SONG PLAYING)

02:48:43.030 --> 02:48:44.906
(OLD JAZZ SONG
CONTINUES PLAYING)

03:00:59.099 --> 03:01:00.725
(METAL CLANGING)
